+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-single-challenge-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe four registered results now have proved compact presentations: #767/PR768 supplies low-degree soundness, and #770/PR773 supplies Pauli completeness plus qudit/qubit soundness. #769/PR772 supplies the exact named-definition extraction frontier. This packet makes a concrete single-file Challenge from that completed mathematical surface, addressing Palomar goal #743.\n\n### Inputs and mathematical invariants\nUse published heads #770/PR7730397cb4512a686cb0d55874af8cfd6f6a559f109, #767/PR768ad84bef98b8259c694fff62436db31236b45e295, and #769/PR7720c51d0a2025354ef155262eedaf2cb754664beee with their inherited parents. MAIN prepares a separate current-main worktree containing these heads before activation. Read the two accepted Astra route reports and the actual four compact theorem types, bridges, and paper labels lem:pauli-completeness, lem:ld-soundness, thm:pauli and cor:pauli-binary.\n\nPreserve all original and compact theorem meanings, hypotheses, parameter domains, quantifier order, once-and-for-all fixedFieldModel/basis/encoding, complete question and answer carriers, all verifier branches, bounded polynomial representatives, unsquared state error and distinct unaveraged squared operator-error sums. Keep raw Pauli prescribed effects and the different LD wrong-form-to-zero convention. No new assumptions, error weakening, arbitrary helper holes, native_decide or axioms. Library proof code remains complete.\n\n### Work\n1. Consolidate the compact Mathlib-only declaration surface into one compiled module under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar, preserving public names, types, values and semantics. Existing definition modules may become thin public re-exports so proved bridges/aliases keep working. Keep proof bridges and headline proof bodies separate. This stabilizes elaboration and generated names for single-file extraction. Start with the six compact definition modules Foundation, LowDegreeGame, Extraction, LowDegreeConsistency, PauliGame and PauliExtraction; inspect actual dependencies and include only what is needed. Do not change the original field contracts, selector construction or original library statements. Necessary explicit naming/elaboration fixes are allowed only when mathematically identical and documented; never weaken the frontier for convenience.\n2. Add a narrowly scoped new comparator configuration/header/footer/expected artifact for the four MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar aliases, reusing the existing extractor/assembler. Set definition_names exactly [MIPStarRE.QPBT.fixedFieldModel]. Preserve its full original type/contract and all unregistered reachable values. The final draft has exactly four theorem holes plus this sole registered definition value hole. Keep historical LDT/QPBT configs and goldens intact except inevitable canonical provenance changes explained by the consolidation.\n3. Generate one standalone Challenge.lean importing only allowed Mathlib/Lean modules, with module/public exposure syntax required by the selected compiler. Hard bounds: <=1000 PHYSICAL lines and <=102400 bytes. Prefer close to300lines/32768bytes when fidelity permits, but do not distort mathematics or hide source behind local imports, compressed encodings, helper proof holes, tricks with generated files or unchecked assumptions. Concise documentation and ordinary formatting are appropriate. Store an intended-sorry golden artifact with a clear .expected suffix, following existing project conventions; no real library proof is renamed or hidden.\n4. Compile the generated standalone file against only the matching pinned Mathlib and verify all four complete library aliases still compile with only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound. Measure physical lines/UTF-8 bytes and actual closure contents. State clearly that a local4.32 prototype is not final Palomar/native verification; the mandatory4.35/native replay and all-library module gates will follow reconciliation. If an existing trusted comparator setup can check exact environment equality locally without changing other worktrees, use it; do not download/build a new verification framework or claim official final CI.\n\n### Scope and acceptance\nOwn new consolidation/generator/artifact files and the compact Palomar definition re-exports only. Do not edit the original mathematical source, parent proof bridge bodies unless strictly necessary for identical interface elaboration, other worktrees, toolchain, or companion clone (owned by754). No full project build; focused new modules/targets and generated Challenge checks. Keep the module-conversion convention. A fresh source check alone does not refresh .olean metadata: build changed dependency modules before extraction.\n\nPublish a narrow stacked library PR with normal hooks, clear parent dependencies, exact source/name/type preservation evidence, no-loss bound statement and honest measurements. MAIN owns source reconciliation, canonical CI, independent review, the final Astra faithfulness review of the actual Challenge, companion\n\n### MAIN integration phase (2026-10-02; #27 comment5942473721)\nThe prototype is now published in PR775 and includes all compact statement, bridge and extractor predecessors. After #756 merges, reconcile and gate the WHOLE main-to-PR775 diff in one integration candidate; no parent approval is presumed. This supersedes the earlier requirement to merge each parent PR separately. Preserve all published parent commits/costs and hold their issues/PRs open until their included work lands in the normally gated integration. Canonical full CI and independent exact-head review must inspect the entire combined diff. The actual Challenge SHA2564600b1c3e2409edf2a68df53a2055516c99646e42750f966cf02e60437700de3 received an independent Astra mathematical audit with no new drift; preserve it or obtain a new hash-bound assessment. Native equality, supported compiler and all final gates remain mandatory.\n",
