+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-final-compact-aliases-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe compact Palomar game and extraction packets must be connected to the three remaining registered results: Pauli completeness, qudit soundness, and qubit soundness. Low-degree soundness already has a proved compact alias in #767/PR768. This packet supplies the remaining exact aliases, so all four statements can later be consolidated into the single Mathlib-only Challenge.\n\n### Mathematical contract\nRead the canonical paper before writing: references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex, lem:pauli-completeness (around1229\u20131234), thm:pauli (1431\u20131445), cor:pauli-binary (1469\u20131491); 04_preliminaries.tex fixed field/basis and qudit/qubit passages; and the actual original public theorem types in Completeness.lean, Soundness.lean and QubitForm.lean. Read the two published Astra Palomar route reports; the second governs fixedFieldModel. No statement change is authorized.\n\nProve MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_spcc_value_one, pauli_soundness, and pauli_soundness_qubit using the completed compact game and exact transport from #766 and the witness/error identities from #763. Preserve the entire original admissible parameter domain through the proved record equivalence. The selected finite field, self-dual normal basis, binary encoding and qubit coordinate map must be the once-and-for-all original fixedFieldModel; no freshly quantified field, chosen transport package or extra assumptions.\n\nCompleteness: for each admissible parameter there exists a symmetric SPCC strategy of value exactly1. Use #766's exact symmetry, positive-support commutation, projectivity, consistency and value transport; no assumed symmetry/game equality.\n\nEach soundness theorem: existential a,b precede all P, epsilon and strategies, with 1\u2264a, 0<b, b<1. The epsilon domain remains0\u2264epsilon and there is no projectivity/SPCC assumption on the strategy. Success remains1\u2212epsilon\u2264value. The witness has finite auxiliary local spaces, local linear isometries and a unit auxiliary vector. Preserve the three distinct conclusions: the unsquared state norm error, Alice's unaveraged sum of squared operator errors, Bob's separate unaveraged sum, each with the exact original deltaQld a b epsilon P.m P.d P.q. Every PauliKind is quantified as before. Do not substitute the sharper sibling's different bound for the registered statement or lose a factor/root in transport.\n\nUse the raw prescribed Pauli-outcome effects, retaining malformed-answer branches. Do not use the low-degree convention of sending wrong-form answers to zero for these effects. The qubit sum remains indexed by the original field outcomes using the original fixed basis. Keep the full ambient question carrier and all seven answer constructors from #766. The compact witness's ideal state/register order/normalization must exactly match the old witness.\n\n### Compact surface and scope\nAdd small concrete Pauli/qubit specializations as needed under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar, keeping Mathlib-only definitions separate from proof bridges. Reuse the generic ExtractionWitness/stateError/operator-error vocabulary and prove relabeling identities rather than defining the new theorem in terms of a converted legacy Strategy. Concrete ideal projectors and lifted effects must be actual definitions with exact checked equalities to the old ones; no conclusion-shaped fields, opaque shortcut, arbitrary proof hole or generic family premise on a headline.\n\nDo not edit the original four theorems, their proof dependencies/bounds, parent packet files, low-degree alias, toolchain or module-conversion packets. If an essential reusable helper is absent, add it in a new bridge file. Pure new modules follow the committed module-conversion pattern; legacy proof bridges may temporarily need old imports pending the scheduled library conversion. Later consolidation will put the compact definition surface in one compiled module to avoid module-local generated-name drift in extraction.\n\nOnly the four final Challenge theorem bodies and the explicitly registered fixedFieldModel value will later be holes. This library packet has no sorry, axiom, native_decide or kernel bypass. Do not replace unchanged public theorem statements merely to reduce the artifact. Aim for a concise specialization/statement surface and report its physical lines/bytes; do not sacrifice fidelity to the preferred size.\n\n### Inputs and gates\nParents are #766 (Pauli game and strategy transport) and #763/PR764 at9899761320c429dfec8ef1b77024501f237af70e (extraction errors), with their inherited #760/#762 parents. #767/PR768 ad84bef98b8259c694fff62436db31236b45e295 is the already completed low-degree alias, available read-only for interface consistency. MAIN supplies an isolated setup worktree with published parent heads before activation. Additive stacked preparation is permitted, but all dependencies and upgrade/module reconciliation must pass normal gates before merge.\n\nAcceptance: focused Lean and target builds for all new files, a focuse\n\n### Incoming transport API note (MAIN,2026-10-02)\nThe published766 strategy bridge will contain pauliSymmetricGame, defined by\nrelabeling the original library SymmetricGame. This is useful proof transport,\nbut it must NOT occur in a compact headline's statement dependency closure:\nits value deliberately retains the legacy game and symmetry proof machinery.\nFor completeness, use the concrete SPCC predicate already permitted by766's\ncontract: projectivity of each measurement, existing compact consistency, and\nexisting IsCommutingOn for the compact pauliQuestionPMF. State this as a small\nMathlib-only definition without a SymmetricGame argument. Prove equivalence\nby unfolding the current IsSPCC and rewriting pauliSymmetricGame_toGame, then\nuse the checked766 conversions. This is an exact presentation change with no\nextra assumptions; no symmetry proof or helper value is made into a hole.\nLikewise, all final value hypotheses name the compact pauliGame, and none of\nthe final statements mention Strategy.toStrategy, library transport wrappers,\nor proof-only bridge constructors. Those stay in the proofs. The sole selected\nfield still uses the original full fixedFieldModel type and original value.\n",
