+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-definition-frontier-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe accepted single-file Palomar route registers exactly MIPStarRE.QPBT.fixedFieldModel as a definition with an unspecified Challenge value. Its full type remains, and the Solution keeps the existing proved construction. The published Astra reports verified official comparator support and measured a potential375-line reduction, but the current extraction script still follows that definition's value. This packet implements the missing artifact-generation support; it is independent of unfinished Pauli proofs.\n\n### Scope\nRead scripts/comparator/README.md, extract_closure.lean, assemble_challenge.py and the challenge config path, plus both published Astra route reports. Extend existing configuration/extraction/assembly minimally to support explicit definition_names with official comparator semantics: traverse every registered definition's full type and its dependencies, stop only its value, preserve all other reachable definition/proof-helper values, and emit a declaration with the same name, universes, binders, return type and safety but an unspecified Challenge value. Reject missing/non-definition names. Preserve the ordinary theorem frontier and all existing behavior when definition_names is absent/empty. No library statement, field choice, source proof or source-file relocation in this packet.\n\nFor the actual QPBT example, permit only the already-approved selector in the example config and keep FieldModel, IsAdmissibleSize and the complete FixedFieldModel contract, including cardinality, algebra, natural binary encoding, self-duality and normality. The unchanged library selector remains the Solution construction. No arbitrary helper-proof erasure or broader assumed interface is justified by this feature. Explain the difference between generated Challenge holes and checked Solution axioms.\n\nDo not activate the new option in existing canonical checked-in QPBT/LDT fixtures: those record the current verified split challenge and must remain byte-identical. Use a separate temporary prototype output for the named-selector experiment. Measure actual extracted dependencies, lines and bytes after compiling the relevant source metadata; identify any leaked construction dependency honestly. A prototype over the old four statements is expected to remain oversized, and is not the final Palomar Challenge or a readiness claim.\n\n### Validation\nAdd meaningful targeted tests showing that registered definition value-only helpers are omitted, type dependencies remain, unregistered definition/proof values remain, bad registered names fail, and the no-option path leaves both current golden fixtures unchanged. Use real Lean extraction for the semantic frontier check where feasible, not only a test mirroring the Python implementation. Run focused existing comparator tests and normal hooks. No full project build; MAIN owns canonical CI and independent review after toolchain reconciliation. Keep the change to existing scripts/tests/docs, no new framework or workflow gate.\n\nPublish a narrow PR with Motivation/Description/Testing, preserved defaults and measured prototype limitations. This is artifact code, not mathematical proof: no theorem assumptions, bounds or permitted-axiom policy changes. No new sorry in library source. Record the final inventory obligation if any executable Lean script needs a module header under packet753.",
