+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-compact-ld-soundness-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe compact low-degree game and exact strategy/value/projectivity bridges are published in #762 / PR765. The single-file Palomar statement still needs the three measurement-consistency conclusions and the theorem with the original quantifier order and error function. This packet supplies that exact compact alias using the already proved library theorem.\n\n### Mathematical contract\nRead the paper's lem:ld-soundness at references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413\u2013440, its measurement convention at394\u2013408, and def:consistency in06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:232\u2013248. Read the actual exists_ld_soundness declaration, consistencyDefect, PolyMeasTuple, evalPolyTupleAt, ldPointQuestionOf, ldPointValuesOrZero and deltaLd. The defect is the off-diagonal sum of Born weights, averaged over the stated question law; do not silently replace it by a norm distance or an unproved1-minus-agreement formula.\n\nAdd compact Mathlib-only definitions for effect-level deterministic postprocessing, polynomial-tuple evaluation, the exact off-diagonal consistency functional, and the three displayed LD defects. An effect-level finite sum is sufficient; avoid pulling unnecessary postprocessed-POVM proof fields into the statement closure. Preserve bounded polynomial representatives, the whole three-summand answer type and the original wrong-form-to-zero point-answer map. The first two defects use uniform points; the third has no substantive question distribution (the Unit uniform law is the existing encoding). Reuse the compact POVM type for both polynomial measurements.\n\nCopy deltaLd exactly, including argument order(a,b,epsilon,q,m,d,k), real powers and the factor a*(d*m*k)^a. Add a proved compact exists_ld_soundness alias in namespace MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar:\nexists a b,1<=a and0<b and b<=1, then for every parameter tuple and epsilon>0, every projective compact strategy with value>=1-epsilon, there exist GA and GB with all three separate defects <= that same deltaLd. Keep that quantifier order and the same a,b; no extra assumption/bridge package, normalization or exponent loss.\n\nUse the exact existing fixedFieldModel family. If quantifying over compact LowDegreeParams, prove its record equivalence to old LdParams in the separate bridge and instantiate the field/encoding from fixedFieldModel at those same q/admissibility fields. Do not quantify over an independent field/basis/encoding, require d<q, or introduce a new selector. Keep the full intrinsic field contract; exactly fixedFieldModel is the eventual allowed definition hole, never a library hole. Prove exact postprocessing/evaluation/consistency identities and transport the existing theorem. Preserve original sources and all original explicit bounds/siblings; this packet changes no source theorem or estimate.\n\n### Files and scope\nUse new compact consistency-definition and theorem/bridge files under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar. Aim for <=110 physical lines of new compact definitions, separate from proof bridges and the theorem proof. Name public instances/helpers. Keep the pure surface transitively Mathlib-only with module/public imports/exposed declarations; legacy bridge imports may await the library conversion, as recorded in final packet753. Reserve MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_ld_soundness for this faithful proved alias. Do not edit parent Foundation/Bridge/LowDegree modules, original library files, roots, blueprint, #766 Pauli game files or #763 extraction files.\n\nMAIN will consolidate the compact definitions into one compiled module before final Challenge extraction. No Challenge/config generation, toolchain changes, Pauli theorem aliases or reproof of the old soundness theorem in this packet. No sorry, axiom, native_decide, proof bypass, added assumption, collapsed error or weakened bound.\n\n### Acceptance\nFocused Lean/target builds, integrity scan, exact paper-versus-Lean assumptions/conclusions/quantifier audit, and normal hooks/PR with Bound strength: exact transport, unchanged constants and exponents. Parent #762 must pass normal gates before merge. MAIN owns canonical full CI, independent review and merge; the final Challenge receives separate Astra faithfulness review.",
