+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-compact-pauli-game-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe accepted Palomar route needs the Pauli basis game's concrete question law and Boolean verifier in a compact statement surface. Generic strategies (#760), the low-degree game (#762), and exact line representatives (#757) provide the necessary parents. This packet implements the Pauli game and exact transport; it does not restate or reprove soundness.\n\n### Mathematical contract\nRead references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1126\u20131491, the two published Astra route reports, and the full current PauliBasisTest.lean and relevant symmetry definitions. Preserve AdmissibleParams and its once-and-for-all selected finite field, encoding and self-dual normal basis. Any generic field/encoding/trace parameters in internal definitions must specialize to those exact existing choices; the final four results gain no quantifier or assumption.\n\nUse finite product/function coordinates and the compact low-degree question maps, retaining the entire original ambient question carrier, including unused coordinates. Retain all seven answer constructors through an explicit bijection, including malformed answers. The question law is uniform on the existing ordered-edge carrier and the whole ambient seed space, then pushed forward through the two concrete maps. There are86 ordered edges:26 loops and both orientations of30 non-loop undirected edges. Do not replace this by a uniform undirected-edge law with a fair orientation coin.\n\nEvery Boolean verifier branch, answer-shape rejection, gamma gate, coordinate encoding, polynomial condition and off-edge default must agree with the old verifier on all transported questions/answers. Prove this exact equality, exact push-forward PMF equality, and value preservation for every compact strategy. Also provide the exact symmetry/support/SPCC transport needed by completeness; no extra hypothesis package may replace those proofs. Raw prescribed Pauli outcome effects remain available unchanged to later soundness aliases; do not fold malformed answers into zero for this game family. All polynomial carriers remain bounded representatives, never polynomial-function quotients.\n\n### Files and scope\nAdd new compact Pauli game definitions and separate library bridges under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar. Definition surface should depend transitively only on Mathlib and the earlier compact vocabulary, and aim for at most300 physical lines with concise mathematical documentation and named public helpers/instances. Use module/public imports/public exposed declarations where dependencies permit. Keep all original sources, field selection, old games/theorems/bounds and parent packet files unchanged. Reuse the generic exact relabel/value transport proved by #762 when its published API is available.\n\nIf SPCC's existing compact SymmetricGame wrapper would pull legacy proof machinery into the statement closure, an equivalent concrete predicate using the existing projectivity, consistency and positive-support commutation definitions is permitted, with a proved exact equivalence. Do not assume symmetry, a value identity, or the desired conclusion. Keep proof-only bridges outside the compact surface. MAIN later consolidates compact definitions into one compiled module before single-file extraction, avoiding module-local auxiliary-name drift.\n\nNo ideal-state/operator-error work (owned by #763), final four theorem aliases, Challenge generation, toolchain port, or original-library module conversion in this packet. No sorry, axiom, native_decide, bypass, altered error or strengthened domain.\n\n### Acceptance\nFocused Lean and target builds, integrity scan, exact source/domain/conclusion audit, and a narrow PR with normal hooks. Bound strength: exact equalities and equivalences, no quantitative loss. MAIN owns full canonical CI, independent review and merge. Additive stacked work may begin on the completed published #762 parent; dependencies must pass their normal gates before this packet merges.",
