+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-compact-errors-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe accepted compact Palomar route needs one small extraction-witness and error vocabulary shared by the qudit and qubit conclusions. The two Astra route reports require exact transport, separate unsquared state norm and summed squared Alice/Bob operator errors, and the existing ideal-state/outcome convention. This packet makes that vocabulary concrete and proves exact bridges; it does not restate a headline theorem.\n\n### Mathematical contract\nRead references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1431\u20131491, 04_preliminaries.tex:1180\u20131228, and the finite norm/operator-distance definitions in 06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex. Read SoundnessDefs.lean, QubitForm.lean, State.lean and the actual four registered theorem types. Implement one generic finite extraction-witness structure parameterized by the target register and local finite spaces (or the compact Strategy), containing auxiliary finite types, local linear isometries, a unit auxiliary state and no error assumptions. Define the actual normalized EPR factor and shuffled auxiliary\u2013EPR vector, the state norm after applying the tensor of local isometries, and the two separately named sums of squared operator norms. These sums have no averaging factor: preserve the actual source definitions. Keep auxiliary register ordering and every normalization exactly.\n\nUse raw prescribed-answer effects in Pauli and qubit comparisons, never the wrong-form-to-zero completed family. Qubit target outcomes remain indexed by the original field outcomes through the existing fixed basis map. Do not alter any projector, chosen field/basis/encoding, coefficient, exponent, root or error parameter. Any generic matrix-family arguments are ordinary definitional parameters, not extra premises on the eventual theorem. Concrete specializations and their equalities to the existing rawPauliOperatorDistanceA/B and qubitOperatorDistanceA/B must be proved, with no assumed transport package.\n\nProve conversions of existing PauliSoundnessWitness and QubitSoundnessWitness to the compact witness, and exact equalities for their ideal states, unsquared state errors, and both operator sums. Use existing exact qudit\u2013qubit identities where relevant, preserving the chosen basis. No need to prove soundness again or produce the final four aliases. No new source theorem, strengthened domain, error merging, inequality weakening, sorry, axiom, native_decide or kernel bypass.\n\n### Files and scope\nAdd a compact Mathlib-only module under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar for the generic witness/ideal-state/error definitions, aiming for <=150 physical lines with concise mathematical docstrings, module/public import/@[expose] public section and named public helpers/instances. Keep library-specific specialization and proof bridges in a separate new module importing existing sources. Do not edit old modules, Foundation.lean/Bridge.lean from #760, or the low-degree game files owned by #762. No Pauli game implementation or final Challenge generation here. MAIN will consolidate all compact statement definitions into one compiled source before final extraction to avoid module-local auxiliary-name drift.\n\n### Acceptance\nBoth new files type-check, exact equalities and statement/domain audit, no proof holes, normal hooks and a narrow PR with Motivation/Description/Testing and Bound strength (exact, no loss). MAIN owns canonical full CI, independent review and merging. Dependency #760 must pass its gate before merge; additive work may proceed in a separate worktree on its published commit517b0b605f756c53320b1f5df964cae31885cbdc. This does not declare that parent reviewed.",
