+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-compact-ld-game-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe accepted Palomar route needs a single Mathlib-only Challenge within 1000 lines/100 KiB. #760 supplies a 134-line compact finite-game/POVM/strategy vocabulary with exact bridges; #757 supplies the exact elementary line representative. This packet replaces the low-degree game's general conditionally-linear/subspace/distribution presentation by compact concrete data, with proved exact equivalence. It preserves the original registered theorem and game.\n\n### Mathematical contract\nRead references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:31\u2013391 and lem:ld-soundness at413\u2013440, the two published Astra route reports, original LowDegreeGame.lean and LowDegreeGameMeasurements.lean. Use the original fixedFieldModel family and numerical LdParams domain, including its current positivity/divisibility constraints. Do not choose a different field, basis or encoding. Keep the full finite question carriers, including unused ambient coordinates, and the full three-constructor answer sum; malformed answers must remain available to strategies and be rejected or postprocessed exactly as before.\n\nDefine the concrete question law as the uniform law on all nine ordered type pairs and the entire ambient seed space, pushed forward through the same two question maps. Use PMF and elementary finite products/functions. For the canonical line representative use #757's exact least-nonzero-coordinate formula, with identity for zero direction. Preserve every predicate branch and every universal line-incidence test, including zero direction. Bounded polynomial representatives remain MvPolynomial.restrictDegree subtypes, never quotient polynomial functions (there is no d<q assumption).\n\nProve exact question-distribution and Boolean win-predicate equalities after the explicit coordinate/answer equivalences, then exact game values for every compact strategy under #760's conversion. Do not add equality/bridge packages as assumptions. A concrete compact game equal to the original through proved reindexing is required, not a definition that merely aliases the old conditional-linear game or its heavy construction. No numerical inequality or bound loss is permitted. No new source theorem, no final soundness alias, no Pauli game work in this packet.\n\n### Files and integration\nAdd Palomar low-degree game definitions and separate bridge proofs. Keep new definitions intended for the Challenge as a compact contiguous source surface, preferably <=180 physical lines, with named public instances/helpers and module/public import/@[expose] public section. Existing parameter/field contracts may be reused with a precise dependency list: the final Challenge will copy those contracts and register exactly fixedFieldModel. Do not copy its construction or any original proof of soundness into the compact surface. No Challenge/Solution regeneration in this packet. MAIN will consolidate the compact vocabulary into one compiled statement module before final extraction to avoid module-local auxiliary-name drift.\n\nLeave all old declarations, original games, parameters, bounds, root imports and conversion-owned files unchanged. Use separate new files under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar; no edits to Foundation.lean or Bridge.lean from #760. Exact helper proofs may live in a separate library bridge module importing old sources. Keep actual proof obligations explicit in the final report if the bound expires; do not publish sorry/axiom/native_decide or weakened interfaces.\n\n### Acceptance\nFocused Lean checks, integrity scan, exact statement/domain audit, normal hooks and a PR with Motivation/Description/Testing and Bound strength: exact equalities, no loss. MAIN owns canonical CI, independent review and merge. Dependencies #760 and #757 must pass their normal gates before this packet merges. Additive preparation may proceed on their published commits in a separate stacked worktree; do not claim those parent PRs have already passed review.",
