+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: palomar-compact-foundation-20261002 -->\n### Motivation\nThe single Mathlib-only Palomar Challenge must fit 1000 physical lines and 100 KiB. The accepted route (tracker #743; Astra reports scout-palomar-faithfulness-route-20261002-01 and -02) retains the full fixed-field contract, registers only fixedFieldModel as a definition hole, and uses compact finite game/strategy definitions with proved exact bridges. This packet implements the generic game/measurement foundation; it does not restate the four paper results yet.\n\n### Scope\nRead the finite-dimensional game/strategy/SPCC definitions in references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex (especially lines 10\u201357,176\u2013180,232\u2013269), then MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/Defs.lean and its immediate dependencies. Add a small Mathlib-only public module under MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/ containing concrete finite-game, POVM, pure unit-state strategy and symmetric-strategy definitions, Born value, projectivity, consistency and SPCC. Add a separate library bridge module with exact conversions to/from the existing generic structures and equality of game values and equivalence of projectivity/SPCC. Use Mathlib PMF for probabilities; existing Distribution.toPMF and avgOver_eq_toPMF_realWeightedSum are exact bridge APIs. Preserve full finite question/answer carriers, all effects, swap invariance and commutation only on positive-probability support. Do not add assumptions to old declarations or change their bodies. No new independent fixed-field selection. Use module/public import/@[expose] public section for new modules. Aim for <=140 physical lines for the eventual Challenge foundation, <=100 columns, with concise mathematical documentation. The separate proof bridge is not part of Challenge.\n\nKeep this additive packet independent of #744/#756 and ongoing original-file conversion ownership. Avoid modifying Games/Defs.lean or existing root imports; build the new modules explicitly. Explain any API issue before broadening this surface. Full generic exact equivalence is the acceptance criterion; no bridges requiring the desired conclusion as an assumption, no sorry/axiom, no native_decide or kernel bypass. Do not invent quantitative weakenings. If a compact foundation cannot fit this budget faithfully, give measured evidence and retain useful exact proofs.\n\n### Acceptance\nFocused Lean compilation, proof-integrity scan, exactness statement audit and normal hooks. Publish a narrow PR with the standard Motivation/Description/Testing sections and Bound strength: exact equalities/equivalences, no loss. MAIN owns full canonical CI, independent review and merging.",
