-  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: error-bounds-report-20260929 -->\n### Motivation\n\nThe owner error-bound aim #727 requires a merged `docs/error-bounds.md` covering the QPBT and native LDT surveys, the two selected improvements, their proved explicit baselines and final gains, the reasons for deferring every other candidate, and an honest same-parameter comparison with Vidick's public `qldErr` at pinned commit286b3ca44f811fa6e37517c04981bc2f164ee6b5.\n\n### Scope\n\nPrepare the report from the completed Astra surveys01/02/03, supplemental benchmark04, independent LDT check06 and final selection05 under `results/telemetry/sessions/scout-727-20260929-*.last.md`. Final selection05 corrects benchmark04's partial-bundle missing-assembly and parsing concerns, and selects exactly two scopes: LDT triangle#728 and QPBT quantitative assembly#729. All other candidates remain unimplemented.\n\nDrafting may proceed while the proofs run, but no proposed bound may be labelled proved or implemented until checked declarations and merge evidence exist. Final report adoption must bind the actual declaration names, exact before/after bounds, PRs, and validation on main after both implementation PRs merge.\n\n### Acceptance\n\n- Plain-language opening, then one complete candidate table per part with baseline, possible gain, cost/risk and implemented/not-implemented status.\n- Proved before/after numbers, declarations and PR links for the two selected results; every other candidate has a specific deferral reason.\n- Native LDT is treated as an independent target, including unchanged corrected sampling hypotheses.\n- Benchmark comparison uses the same parameters and state/operator distance normalization, reports both better/worse regimes and the completed-vs-raw-answer distinction, and does not turn source inspection into a claim of a benchmark build.\n- No changes to Lean, old theorem statements, paused documentary work, comparator, benchmark code, QKD or LionSR/MIPStarRE.\n- Final report reviewed and merged after the implementation evidence is available, before the requested keeper stop and goal pause.",
