-  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: error-bounds-qpbt-explicit-20260929 -->\n### Motivation\n\nPart of owner quantitative error-bound aim #727. The current QPBT Pauli soundness proof has numerical witnesses hidden behind existential interfaces. The surveys independently trace the current final exponent to `1/5242880000` and provide an explicit closed numerical coefficient. Before strengthening the headline, prove an explicit baseline from these CURRENT proof witnesses.\n\nPrimary paper sources: references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex (`lem:ld-soundness`) and 14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex (`lem:qld-unitary`, final Pauli isometry argument). Existing public soundness and qubit statements, all13 audit entries, and the raw prescribed-answer conclusions remain unchanged.\n\n### Scope\n\nPhase1 is fixed-witness baseline exposure only: kernel-prove the Pauli edge cardinality86, expose the current point/line/global-pair/extraction/transfer constants, and prove explicit baseline siblings of `pauli_soundness` and `pauli_soundness_qubit`. Numerical formulas and exact locations are in `results/telemetry/sessions/scout-727-20260929-01.last.md` and independently in03. This is required baseline work, not an additional selected improvement. Do not obtain a supposed fixed coefficient merely by destructuring an opaque existential theorem.\n\nThe second and last improvement slot is being finalized by the independent Astra selection in #727. The leading mechanism is to retain separate state and operator errors through extraction and transfer, with explicit scalar propagation. Main will record the final selected bound and proof plan before authorizing phase2. Do not independently add other survey candidates.\n\n### Acceptance\n\n- Phase1: explicit current-proof baseline theorems and qubit form, source-aware documentation, preserved old statements/definitions, and successful added axiom-audit entries before any improved proof.\n- Phase2: the selected strictly better explicit headline, all original hypotheses/conclusions, before/after comparison on the correct domain, and necessary propagation only.\n- Zero sorry or new axioms; full local CI, independent mathematical review, exact-head gated merge; one PR for this improvement including baseline work.\n- No changes to benchmark code, paused documentary work, QKD, LionSR/MIPStarRE or the comparator checkout.\n\nMain owns admission, publication and selection. Baseline work can proceed independently of the new LDT theorem in #728; any later consumer of that theorem must use a published exact parent commit and fresh gates.",
+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: qpbt-structural-fixed-ldt-implementation-20260929 -->\n\n**Execution status, 2026-09-30:** Deferred under the owner\u2019s renewed 1\u20132 improvement stopping rule. The mathematical target and full implementation plan below are preserved for later work. This run finishes #728/#729 and the report plus bound ledger in #730, then pauses; no #735 proof worker is admitted. The scheduling statements below describe the preserved follow-up plan.\n\n### Motivation\n\nThe owner requested a substantive improvement to the QPBT part of the source paper with LDT fixed, to implement after the current quantitative implementation #729. The completed survey #733 and an independent Astra referee select one coherent mechanism: preserve squared failure amplitudes and use complete-measurement consistency estimates throughout the existing QPBT constructions. The owner-facing overview is pinned as #734.\n\nThe [full survey](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/2814d000e9c6127bc4d5d30a2ee3f5fe4eb6edc9/results/telemetry/sessions/scout-733-20260929-01.last.md) derives equations (1)\u2013(19). The [independent referee](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/ac0e8ed88fb5400acee65d0a1eaa8a73bf862a8b/results/telemetry/sessions/scout-733-20260929-02.last.md) accepts the complete mathematical plan with no coefficient correction, counterexample or additional public hypothesis. These new results remain unformalized.\n\n### Selected target and frozen input\n\nImplementation begins only after #729 is merged and its actual exact-head structured/canonical/qubit statements and axiom audits are checked. That result supplies the nearer proved baseline, rather than a merely projected baseline.\n\nLet $n=md$, $e=\\min(\\varepsilon,1)$ and $E_b=e^b+q^{-b}+2^{-bn}$. Prove the common bound\n\n$$\\min\\left(4,10^{10}n^{15/4+5/262144}E_{1/1048576}\\right).$$\n\nAlso prove the simpler $n^4$ corollary and the `deltaQld 100 (1/1048576)` corollary, together with the exact qubit counterpart of each of these three bounds (six forms in total). Retain one common witness, the unsquared state norm and both raw prescribed-answer summed-squared operator distances for every basis. Prove comparison with the actual #729 baseline on the clipped/nonnegative domain, including strict improvement in the nontrivial regime.\n\nThe final exponent gain relative to the #729 target is 64, with the same LDT black box on both sides:\n\n- `deltaLd 30 (1/8192)`;\n- extended dimension $2m+2$;\n- sampling parameter $2560000(2m+2)^3d$;\n- unchanged LDT hypotheses, numerical constants and error function.\n\nNo native LDT source, export, blueprint or paper-mirror changes. Preserve the frozen `MIPStarRE/LDT` tree `ddd92480c55bbabba5a96af96064fc792a5eb68c` and every existing definition/error function and theorem statement, including all results introduced by #729. All improvements are additive declarations.\n\n### Mathematical implementation\n\n1. Adapt the complete-measurement identity and three-step consistency triangle to QPBT's vector-state API. Add the projective replacement estimate $C(P,B)\\le R+2\\delta$ from $D(P,A)\\le R$ and $C(A,B)\\le\\delta$. Do not extend these to arbitrary submeasurements.\n2. Prove the projective post-measurement fine/coarse collision and pinching estimates, deriving the new pasting bound $307\\delta+16\\eta$ for the same sandwich when **both** codeword measurements are projective. Construct the Schmidt mirror internally, preserve its question dependence, and retain the conditional collision law. The actual consumer is X-outer: $G_1=Z,G_2=X$ with swapped answer order. Preserve the existing general pasting theorem.\n3. Propagate linear commuting estimates through the existing point construction, retaining both players and every directed comparison; no register-symmetry assumption.\n4. Propagate projective pasting through conditioning and the existing extended-line argument. Update both same-line passing comparisons and all seven branches. Keep the discarded mass and `none`-answer contributions.\n5. Improve rounding transport with the same rounded measurements, chosen before postprocessing maps and comparison families. Thread the result through polynomial separation and completion to construct the actual global pair.\n6. Reuse #729's same-witness extraction, isometry-range, Naimark and raw-effect transfers. Handle zero error, large error, $md/q\\ge1$ and $md=1$ internally, and assemble all required headlines and qubit forms.\n\nThe survey/referee specify the supported intermediate bounds: point error at most $10^{15}e^{1/4}$; paired-line error at most $3\\cdot10^{18}(e^{1/4}+md/q)$; extended-line error at most $10^9m(e^{1/16}+(md/q)^{1/4})$; direct passing error at most $10^{16}m(e^{1/16}+(md/q)^{1/4})$; and rounding consistency at most $660\\lambda^{1/4}+12\\lambda$. The complete derivation, not this list alone, is the implementation authority.\n\n### Source faithfulness and validation\n\nThe source-level improvements are linear consistency calculus, linear twisted commutation and linear projective pasting. The passing and same-space rounding improvements also remove losses in the checked realization. The 64-fold number compares explicit formalization envelopes, not two printed paper exponents. At fixed numerical LDT output $\\lambda$, the proposed checked route has $\\lambda^{1/8}$ dependence; do not advertise this as beating the source's displayed $\\lambda^{1/4}$ Naimark route.\n\nKeep the exact current arbitrary-strategy/AdmissibleParams/nonnegative-error headline domain. Add no supplied-witness, small-error, projective-strategy, legal-answer-support or new divisibility hypothesis. Preserve raw effects, actual range projections and common auxiliary states. Zero proof holes, new axioms or kernel bypasses; all original and new headline axiom audits must pass.\n\nOne implementation PR, with complete separate blueprint correspondence for new mathematics, full canonical local CI, independent Astra review at the exact head, and the normal merge gate with no override. Main will authorize bounded Sol implementation assignments after the prerequisite is met. No implementation is admitted by this issue alone.\n\nThe final report #730 must record this result and all alternatives, source-versus-formalization distinctions, actual before/after numbers, declarations, PRs, validation, and the updated public benchmark comparison. Keep pinned #734 current. Pause only after the expanded owner scope and final report are completed.",
