-  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: error-bounds-ldt-triangle-20260929 -->\n### Motivation\n\nPart of owner error-bound aim #727. The LDT paper's `thm:main-formal` (references/ldt-paper/test_definition.tex:180\u2013202) and the current Lean `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.mainFormal` use the bound\n\n`100000 k^2 m^4 [eps^(1/40000) + (d/q)^(1/40000) + exp(-k/(2560000 m^2))]`.\n\nThe formal theorem has the documented sampling domain `k >= 400 m d`, `k > 0`; both that domain and every existing statement must be preserved. This task prepares the independently surveyed complete-measurement triangle improvement. Main will admit implementation after adopting the final mathematical checks.\n\n### Proposed additive result\n\nFirst prove an explicit baseline corollary, then a new theorem with the same two projective polynomial measurement witnesses and all three consistency conclusions at\n\n`min 1 (10000 k^(1/4) m^(1/2) [eps^(1/8192) + (d/q)^(1/8192) + exp(-k/(640000 m^2))])`.\n\nFor complete measurements, the identity `2 C(A,B) = D(A,B) + u(A) + u(B)` and the three-step squared-distance triangle imply `C(A,D) <= 3(C(A,B)+C(B,C)+C(C,D))`. Apply this at the two final-theorem consistency steps while retaining the existing completion and repaired line-169 errors. Completeness and compatibility of all witnesses must be checked, not assumed. Preserve all boundary cases, including `d=0`, `k>q`, and large error.\n\nThe proof plan and candidate inventory are in `results/telemetry/sessions/scout-727-20260929-02.last.md`, with independent scalar comparison in `scout-727-20260929-03.last.md`. Final cross-track selection and the focused triangle referee are separate Astra assignments. No new bound is claimed proved by this issue.\n\n### Acceptance\n\n- Baseline first, then a proved strictly better headline with the same public hypotheses and all conclusions; no sorry or new axioms.\n- All existing statements, error definitions, and audit entries retained; add new headline audits and accurate separate blueprint entries.\n- Focused Lean checks, full local CI, independent mathematical review, and exact-head gated merge.\n- One PR for this selected improvement; record before/after numbers and declarations for `docs/error-bounds.md`.\n- Do not implement the other surveyed improvements or touch paused documentary work, benchmark code, QKD, LionSR/MIPStarRE, or the comparator checkout.",
+  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: owner-structural-error-findings-20260929 -->\nThis is the owner-requested overview of the most significant structural improvements found in the surveys. The main gains concern error exponents and parameter scaling.\n\n| Track | Selected improvement | Before \u2192 after | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Native LDT | Use a linear consistency estimate for complete measurements and retain fractional powers through the final construction. | Prefactor dependence $k^2m^4\\to k^{1/4}m^{1/2}$; error exponent $1/40000\\to1/8192$; tail denominator $2560000m^2\\to640000m^2$. | **Proved and merged in [PR #731](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/731).** |\n| QPBT, with LDT fixed | Propagate squared failure amplitudes through commutation, projective pasting, passing consistency and rounding. | Proposed final exponent $1/67108864\\to1/1048576$: **64-fold additional gain** over the proved #729 common bound. | **Independently checked mathematically; implementation [#735](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/735) is deferred under the owner\u2019s renewed 2026-09-30 stopping rule. Not yet Lean-proved.** |\n\nThe [QPBT implementation #729](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/729), published in [PR #736](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/736) at `6ea9f96bd86aaaad613130dea49eefdf6e80c5a9`, proves native error propagation, separate state/operator component estimates and the fractional-dimensional bound $H$ below. Its error exponent improves from the proved baseline `1/5242880000` to `1/67108864` (a factor of 78.125). The common polynomial factor improves from the earlier quadratic envelope to $10769120m^{20481/262144}d^{1/64}$. Exact qubit counterparts, the stronger-to-weaker comparisons, and the historical degree-two, degree-four and canonical forms remain available.\n\n[PR #736](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/736) **merged** as [`0b847308`](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/commit/0b847308c30769be983bbd05c297e1014db76590). R4 approved the mathematics; the [owner-admitted scoped fifth review](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/736#pullrequestreview-5372895844) approved the final dependency/docstring patch with no findings and independently verified unchanged Lean code and formulas. The merged head passed all eight fresh CI checks (567 summed step-seconds), all nine CI contexts, 2,187 blueprint axiom checks and 2,198 synchronized declaration checks. All normal merge gates passed; no override was used.\n\n[Owner decision](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/27#issuecomment-5921008674); [two-line merged improvement note](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/27#issuecomment-5921191213). The final report and separate ledger are merged in #742.\n\n**The report and separate bound ledger are merged in [PR #742](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/742)** as [`1b32dfe5`](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/commit/1b32dfe5883ee078e44bcc4d8e1bc38509c51d3a): **16 LDT candidates, 31 QPBT candidates, and 152 stage rows**, including all 57 bound rows from #736. The exact-head documentation CI passed; [normal R2](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/742#pullrequestreview-5375046975) and [independent mathematical R2](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/742#issuecomment-5924825278) both approved with no findings. All normal merge gates passed. [Read the report](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/main/docs/error-bounds.md) and [bound ledger](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/main/docs/bound-ledger-qpbt.md). The bounded two-improvement goal is finished; #735 and kit adoption #741 remain separate future work, and inherited #727 backlog is explicit.\n\nThe adapter correction recovers the stronger error estimate already proved by the unchanged native LDT theorem. The #735 survey separately fixes the full numerical LDT input shown below; its source-argument improvement remains a distinct, deferred result.\n\nThe #735 mathematical plan is preserved as a deferred follow-up, with the same LDT theorem, hypotheses, numerical constants and sampling parameter on both sides. The current mathematical run completes #728/#729 and the report plus bound ledger, then stops the keeper and pauses under the owner\u2019s stopping rule. The latest owner instruction places kit adoption [#741](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/741) in a **separate future goal or session**, estimated at about one working day; it will not be inserted before this pause. The [measured v0.5 migration steps](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/741#issuecomment-5916397375) are posted. The future adoption session must verify that the owner has published the v0.5 tag before starting; v0.4 must not be adopted.\n\nThe **64-fold number compares explicit formalization bounds**. The source paper leaves its final exponent existential. The improvements to the source argument itself are the stronger consistency estimate, linear twisted commutation, and linear projective pasting; the survey distinguishes these from improvements to the checked direct-game and rounding realization.\n\n[Read the complete survey and candidate ranking](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/2814d000e9c6127bc4d5d30a2ee3f5fe4eb6edc9/results/telemetry/sessions/scout-733-20260929-01.last.md). Tracking: [survey #733](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/733), [final report #730](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/730). [Read the independent mathematical acceptance](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/ac0e8ed88fb5400acee65d0a1eaa8a73bf862a8b/results/telemetry/sessions/scout-733-20260929-02.last.md). Follow-up implementation: [#735](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/issues/735).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Native LDT: proved bounds, domain and evidence</summary>\n\nWriting $r=d/q$, the proved baseline is\n\n$$100000k^2m^4\\left[\\varepsilon^{1/40000}+r^{1/40000}+e^{-k/(2560000m^2)}\\right].$$\n\nThe merged improvement is\n\n$$\\min\\left(1,10000k^{1/4}m^{1/2}\\left[\\varepsilon^{1/8192}+r^{1/8192}+e^{-k/(640000m^2)}\\right]\\right).$$\n\nBoth use the same current formalized domain, including $k\\ge400md$ and $k>0$, and retain the same two projective polynomial measurements and all three consistency conclusions. The earlier discrepancy with the paper's printed $k\\ge md$ is not eliminated by this improvement.\n\nDeclarations:\n\n- `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.main_formal_explicit_baseline`\n- `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.main_formal_linear_triangle_bound`\n- `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.mainFormalLinearTriangleError_le_min_mainFormalError`\n- `MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.mainFormalLinearTriangleError_lt_min_mainFormalError`\n\n[PR #731](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/pull/731) merged as `fac99fdf22bbdbb83a2376ca48cd679dc7d13750` after full local CI and independent mathematical/code and prose review at head `df8f6bc9255e7aa524ceebff3bffc0087dfc1ee2`. Both axiom-audit targets passed. The strict comparison theorem states its nontrivial regime explicitly.\n\nThe survey also records further structural LDT opportunities: a multiplicative Bernoulli tail changing quadratic to linear dimension dependence in the decay denominator, linear accumulation over dimensions, and stronger commutativity estimates. Self-improvement and incomplete-measurement pasting require additional mathematics; complete-measurement identities cannot simply be reused without controlling missing mass.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>QPBT: proposed gain with the LDT input fixed</summary>\n\nThe central new pasting estimate is\n\n$$C(A,\\operatorname{paste}(G_1,G_2))\\le307\\delta+16\\eta,$$\n\nwhen **both** codeword measurements are projective, as they are in the QPBT application. The current explicit bound is $115(\\eta^{1/4}+\\delta^{1/8})$. The general source lemma, which assumes less projectivity, keeps its existing statement.\n\nThe selected mechanism combines this estimate with the complete-measurement consistency identity and projective replacement estimates. It uses the same sandwich measurements, rounding construction and extraction witness. It retains raw prescribed-answer effects and the isometry/Naimark range terms.\n\nPut $n=md$, $e=\\min(\\varepsilon,1)$ and $E_b=e^b+q^{-b}+2^{-bn}$. The earlier locally proved #729 bound is\n\n$$\\min(4,10^{14}n^4E_{1/67108864}).$$\n\nThe degree-two correction is now proved at commit `2ad0a5c1`:\n\n$$I=\\min(4,10^9n^2E_{1/67108864}).$$\n\nIt reconstructs the witness in its larger nonsaturated region and preserves the raw-operator and state metrics. A separate proved mixed component theorem retains the native-adapter error and its distinct state/operator terms. No comparison between that mixed function and the deferred #735 function is claimed.\n\nThe published #736 source at `6ea9f96b` preserves this proved endpoint:\n\n$$H=\\min(4,10769120\\,m^{20481/262144}d^{1/64}E_{1/67108864}).$$\n\nThis retains fractional powers of the dimensions instead of the current quadratic factor, with the same error exponent. The accepted mathematical calculation also keeps six native-error contributions separate and removes the coarse comparison from the construction of the witness. **This endpoint is proved and merged in #736 after full CI, R4 mathematical approval and the admitted scoped fifth review.** The comparison $H\\le I\\le C$ is proved, where $C$ is the historical degree-four bound. A new algebraic comparison, checked by main, shows that $H$ and the deferred #735 function $F$ are **incomparable**: exact admissible families give both $H<F<4$ and $F<H<4$. Thus the stronger exponent in #735 does not give uniform dominance over the proved fractional dimension powers. These are comparisons of the displayed scalar functions. The final report and ledger are merged in #742. [Read the exact families and cap analysis](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/cdc7a3c9b2f2a6bd1f284c0e2d3f0d2e199c9715/results/telemetry/sessions/scout-730-20261001-01.last.md). [Read the accepted repair calculation](https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT/blob/ddedd75181c6889f4d8b40d7a9620b5a488c293f/results/telemetry/sessions/scout-729-20261001-01.last.md).\n\nThe additional proposed #735 target is\n\n$$\\min(4,10^{10}n^4E_{1/1048576}).$$\n\nA slightly sharper derived dimension power is $p=15/4+5/262144<4$. The coefficient reduction is secondary; the main gain is removal of root losses. The final unsquared state norm still requires a square root.\n\nThe same LDT input is used throughout: `deltaLd 30 (1/8192)`, extended dimension $2m+2$, and native sample $2560000(2m+2)^3d$. The same LDT function is evaluated at the improved passing error; neither its theorem nor its numerical constants change.\n\nThe deferred implementation plan calls for the sharper fractional-power form\n\n$$\\min(4,10^{10}n^{15/4+5/262144}E_{1/1048576}),$$\n\nthen derive the simpler $n^4$ form above, the canonical error-function form, and the exact qubit versions.\n\nThe source argument and the established formal construction must be distinguished. At the same numerical LDT output $\\lambda$, the selected formal route improves $\\lambda^{1/16}$ to $\\lambda^{1/8}$. This does **not** improve on the source's displayed Naimark route $\\lambda^{1/4}$; the extra rounding loss belongs to the current formal realization. The new source-argument estimates remain the linear complete-measurement consistency, twisted commutation, and projective pasting bounds described above.\n\nThe survey ranks this as the strongest fully derived coherent improvement found with LDT fixed, not as a claim of global optimality. It is independently accepted mathematics; Lean implementation and its normal CI, axiom audits, and independent review remain deferred under #735; they are outside the current run\u2019s renewed stopping rule.\n\n</details>\n",
