+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Upgrade the project for issue #756 to the admitted Palomar minimum after the module-conversion pilot.\n- Keep every theorem statement, source domain, and quantitative bound unchanged while restoring compatibility with Lean/Mathlib v4.35.0-rc2.\n\n### Description\n- Pin Lean and Mathlib to `v4.35.0-rc2`; the authenticated Mathlib revision is `065356127b1dc0016f66b7283ce0ce2c4055aa55` with its matching transitive manifest.\n- Repair required rc2 API, tactic, generated-instance, and elaboration-transparency incompatibilities. Explicit finite instances are extensionally unchanged; reducibility annotations affect elaboration only and do not alter declaration types.\n- Port the comparator extractor to the rc2 slice-based string API and regenerate both canonical fixtures. The LDT fixture changes only one source-provenance line; its declarations and target statement are unchanged.\n- Update current version documentation and the dated operations evolution record. Historical reports are untouched.\n- Resolve review findings F1 and F2 on the final port: remove the generic decide wrapper in `BranchComparison.lean`, apply core `@of_decide_eq_true` directly with the predicate's classical decision procedure, and restore the continuation indentation in `NaimarkReduction.lean`. No mathematical statement or expression changed.\n\n### Testing\n- Focused checks for every repaired root, including the ExtendedLineGame transparency frontier.\n- Serialized helper-managed full build: all 9,633 jobs passed (`worktree-build-20261002T043941Z-2817385.log`).\n- `lake build MIPStarRE.LDT.Test.AxiomAudit MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.AxiomAudit` passed (9,593 jobs).\n- Comparator regeneration and clean drift check passed for LDT and QPBT; all 10 comparator tests passed.\n- Installed-hook check, changed-statement audit, proof-bypass scan, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Normal pre-commit hook passed (897 tests total, 9 skipped, 888 executed), followed by statement-integrity audits.\n- Review repair: focused `lake env lean` checks passed for `BranchComparison.lean` and `NaimarkReduction.lean`; both files passed the proof-hole/bypass scan, `git diff --check`, the normal pre-commit integrity hook, and checked pre-push publication.\n- No new full CI or review was run for the repair commit; MAIN retains the exact-head gates.\n\n### Bound strength\n- No estimate statement, exponent, coefficient, error definition, theorem domain, or mathematical bound changed.\n\n---\nCloses #756\n",
