+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Complete the single-file Palomar prototype requested by #774 from the four\n  proved compact aliases and the named-definition extraction frontier.\n- This branch is stacked on the frozen published heads for PR #768\n  (`ad84bef98b8259c694fff62436db31236b45e295`), PR #772\n  (`0c51d0a2025354ef155262eedaf2cb754664beee`), and PR #773\n  (`0397cb4512a686cb0d55874af8cfd6f6a559f109`). Those parent gates remain\n  prerequisites for merge.\n\n### Description\n- Consolidate the six compact Mathlib-only definition modules into\n  `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.Definitions`; retain the original module paths as thin\n  public re-exports. The six declaration bodies are text-identical after\n  blank-line normalization. Explicit `MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind` annotations in\n  `ExtractionBridge` preserve the names those binders resolved to before the\n  consolidated public re-export.\n- Add the `palomar` comparator configuration for exactly the four compact\n  aliases and exactly one registered definition,\n  `MIPStarRE.QPBT.fixedFieldModel`. Add an opt-in provenance-comment switch;\n  historical LDT and QPBT generation remains byte-for-byte current.\n- Check in one monolithic Mathlib-only expected artifact with 992 physical\n  lines, 52,483 UTF-8 bytes, and SHA-256\n  `4600b1c3e2409edf2a68df53a2055516c99646e42750f966cf02e60437700de3`.\n  Its extracted closure has 183 rows: 157 ranged declarations, 26 generated\n  declarations, and one `DEF_SAFE` definition frontier. The only holes are the\n  four theorem bodies and the `fixedFieldModel` value.\n- This is a Lean 4.32 prototype. Lean 4.35 native replay, exact-environment\n  comparison, all-library module gates, and final publication remain for MAIN's\n  reconciliation work.\n\n### Testing\n- `lake env lean` on `Definitions.lean`, all six re-export modules, and\n  `ExtractionBridge.lean`.\n- Focused `lake build` of the compact Palomar definitions, bridges, and all\n  three headline modules. No full project build was run, as required by #774.\n- `lake env lean /tmp/palomar-compact/Challenge.lean` succeeds with exactly five\n  intended `sorry` warnings.\n- Comparator drift checks pass for `ldt`, `qpbt`, and `palomar`; the historical\n  LDT and QPBT goldens are unchanged.\n- The normal pre-commit hook passed 908 script tests plus statement-origin,\n  proof-debt, conclusion-shaped-hypothesis, unfaithful-marker, and explicit\n  axiom audits.\n- `#print axioms` for all four completed compact aliases reports exactly\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n\n## Statement integrity\n- The four public compact theorem declarations were not edited. Their footer\n  statements match the library statement text exactly: `lem:pauli-completeness`,\n  `lem:ld-soundness`, `thm:pauli`, and `cor:pauli-binary` retain their complete\n  hypotheses, carriers, quantifier order, verifier branches, and conclusions.\n- Verdict: exact. No assumptions were added and no conclusion was weakened or\n  strengthened.\n\n## Bound strength\n- No estimate statement or proof changed. The unsquared state error and the\n  separate unaveraged squared Alice/Bob operator-error sums remain distinct,\n  and all numerical error functions are preserved verbatim.\n\n---\nCloses #774\n",
