+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Complete #770 by connecting the compact Palomar game and extraction surfaces to\n  `lem:pauli-completeness`, `thm:pauli`, and `cor:pauli-binary`.\n- This change is stacked on #763 / PR #764 at\n  `9899761320c429dfec8ef1b77024501f237af70e` and #766 / PR #771 at\n  `531cd4ca281b4b8e6d558a881cbd1e29a86eee61`; both parent PRs must merge first.\n\n### Description\n- Add a concrete Mathlib-only Palomar Pauli extraction surface: compact strategy and\n  register specializations, the concrete SPCC predicate, the exact `deltaQld`, raw\n  qudit and qubit effects, ideal projectors, and separate Alice and Bob errors.\n- Add exact proof bridges for admissible parameters, strategies, witnesses, effects,\n  projectors, and all three extraction errors. The original `fixedFieldModel` remains\n  the sole selected field and basis.\n- Prove `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_spcc_value_one`,\n  `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.pauli_soundness`, and\n  `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.pauli_soundness_qubit` with compact public statements and\n  proof-only transport confined to theorem bodies.\n- Add four files totaling 651 physical lines and 29,241 bytes. Original theorem files,\n  parent packet files, and the existing low-degree alias are unchanged.\n\n### Testing\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/PauliExtraction.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/PauliExtractionBridge.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/PauliCompleteness.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/PauliSoundness.lean`\n- `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.PauliCompleteness MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.PauliSoundness`\n- `rg -n \"sorry|admit|axiom\"` over all four new files returned no matches.\n- A focused `#print axioms` audit reports exactly\n  `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` for each of the three aliases.\n- `scripts/install_git_hooks.sh --check` and all milestone pre-commit hooks passed.\n- A full `lake build` was intentionally not run: the issue activation assigns this\n  worker focused target checks and reserves canonical full CI for MAIN.\n\n### Statement integrity\n- Paper assumptions: the original admissible Pauli parameter domain; for soundness,\n  existential constants precede the parameters, nonnegative error, an arbitrary\n  strategy, and the original success inequality.\n- Lean assumptions: the compact `PauliParams` record contains the same data and a\n  redundant positivity proof field, with a proved bidirectional equivalence to the\n  registered admissible record. No projectivity, SPCC, transport package, or generic\n  proof premise is added to either soundness theorem.\n- Paper conclusions: completeness gives a symmetric projective, consistent,\n  positive-support commuting value-one strategy; soundness gives finite auxiliary\n  spaces, local linear isometries, a unit auxiliary vector, an unsquared state error,\n  and separate unaveraged Alice and Bob sums of squared operator errors for every\n  Pauli kind.\n- Lean conclusions: the same conclusions use the compact game and extraction\n  vocabulary, the original fixed field and basis, raw Pauli outcome effects, and the\n  exact registered `deltaQld`. The qubit sums remain indexed by field outcomes.\n- Verdict: exact under the proved record equivalence, with only a faithful redundant\n  boundary proof field.\n\n### Bound strength\n- `Palomar.deltaQld`: stated formula equals the registered formula by reflexivity;\n  disposition: sharp.\n- `Palomar.pauli_soundness`: each state, Alice, and Bob bound is transported with the\n  same `deltaQld`, coefficient, exponent, root, and normalization; disposition: sharp.\n- `Palomar.pauli_soundness_qubit`: the same three exact bounds are transported through\n  the fixed-basis qubit specialization; disposition: sharp.\n- No bound weakening or deferred loss is introduced.\n\n### Dependencies\n- #763 / PR #764 supplies the generic extraction witness and exact error identities.\n- #766 / PR #771 supplies the compact Pauli game, strategy transport, and value and\n  SPCC transport facts.\n\n---\nCloses #770\n",
