+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Issue #769 needs the comparator challenge generator to support the approved `MIPStarRE.QPBT.fixedFieldModel` definition frontier without changing theorem statements, field data, or existing fixtures.\n- The official comparator compares a registered definition type and safety while the Solution axiom audit still checks its implementation value.\n\n### Description\n- Add optional `definition_names` configuration, validate registered names as repository-local definitions, traverse their complete types, and stop only their values.\n- Preserve the source declaration name, universes, binders, return type, and safety while generating a Challenge-only `by sorry`; all unregistered definition and proof values remain in the closure.\n- Keep both canonical configs and expected fixtures unchanged when the option is absent or empty.\n- Document the temporary fixed-field prototype: 31 files, 3,509 lines, 161,038 bytes, and 252 dependencies versus 3,956 lines, 181,818 bytes, and 275 dependencies for the current four-target tree. The 23 removed dependencies are construction-only; no prototype-only dependency appeared.\n- Record that the unchanged Solution still uses `Classical.choice (exists_fixed_field_model q hq)`, that the prototype remains above both Palomar hard limits, and that `extract_closure.lean` belongs in packet #753 module-header inventory.\n\n### Testing\n- `python3 -m unittest scripts.tests.test_assemble_challenge scripts.tests.test_comparator_challenge_config scripts.tests.test_comparator_challenge_drift` (47 tests).\n- Normal pre-commit hook: 904 script tests passed, 9 skipped.\n- `python3 scripts/comparator/check_challenge_drift.py --root .` (LDT and 31-file QPBT fixtures current).\n- `lake env lean scripts/comparator/extract_closure.lean` with frontier variables unset (70 ordinary rows, zero hole rows).\n- Temporary real-metadata QPBT extraction with only `MIPStarRE.QPBT.fixedFieldModel` registered; measured declaration and size inventory documented above.\n- `python3 -m py_compile ...` and `git diff --check`.\n- No full project build; issue #756 owns toolchain reconciliation and canonical CI/review.\n\n---\nCloses #769\n",
