+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Implement #767 by exposing paper `lem:ld-soundness` on the compact Palomar low-degree game surface.\n- Reuse the exact game, value, and projectivity bridges from #762 / PR #765 and the proved library theorem at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413-440`.\n\n### Description\n- Add a 109-line Mathlib-only compact module for deterministic effect postprocessing, bounded polynomial-tuple evaluation, the exact off-diagonal consistency functional, the three displayed low-degree defects, and `deltaLd`.\n- Prove exact parameter, postprocessing, evaluation, distribution, strategy-effect, and defect identities against the registered low-degree library.\n- Add `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_ld_soundness` with the paper's quantifier order, the existing `fixedFieldModel`, the same universal constants `a,b`, and all three separate conclusions.\n\n### Testing\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/LowDegreeConsistency.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/LowDegreeConsistencyBridge.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/LowDegreeSoundness.lean`\n- `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.LowDegreeSoundness`\n- Integrity scan over all three files found no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, proof bypass, or debugging tokens.\n- Normal pre-commit hooks passed for all three milestones. Per the packet contract, MAIN owns the canonical full `lake build` and independent review.\n\n## Statement integrity\n- Paper assumptions: admissible `(q,m,d,k)` with positive `m,d,k`, `m | q`, `\u03b5 > 0`, and a projective strategy succeeding with probability at least `1 - \u03b5`.\n- Lean assumptions: exactly the compact `LowDegreeParams`, `\u03b5 > 0`, compact projectivity, and compact value bound, using the globally selected `fixedFieldModel`.\n- Paper conclusion: polynomial measurements for Alice and Bob satisfying the two uniform-point consistency bounds and the distribution-free polynomial consistency bound.\n- Lean conclusion: exactly those three separate off-diagonal Born-weight defects, each bounded by the same `deltaLd`.\n- Verdict: exact.\n\n## Bound strength\n- `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.deltaLd`: stated `a * (d*m*k)^a * (\u03b5^b + q^(-b) + 2^(-(b*(m*d))))`; the proof gives the identical registered expression. Disposition: sharp.\n- `MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_ld_soundness`: all three defects retain the original constants and exponents with the same `a,b`; transport is by equality only. Disposition: sharp.\n\n---\nCloses #767\n",
