+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Complete #762 with the compact Mathlib-only low individual degree game required by the Palomar route.\n- Preserve the paper domain and the existing `LdParams` field model, question law, answer carrier, and verifier from `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:31-440`.\n- Depends on #760 at published commit `517b0b605f756c53320b1f5df964cae31885cbdc` and #757 at published commit `03f79f4dd780d1d9feac5e7b50b9f97a94e0d634`; this PR must not merge before both pass their normal gates.\n\n### Description\n- Add a 177-line public compact game surface using the full ambient product space, all nine ordered question-type pairs, the complete three-summand answer type, and `MvPolynomial.restrictDegree` representatives.\n- Use the published least-nonzero-coordinate line representative, including identity at zero direction.\n- Prove exact question-coordinate, PMF, answer, and Boolean verifier equivalences with the registered `ldGame`.\n- Relabel compact POVMs, games, and strategies along equivalences; prove exact preservation of Born weights, projectivity, and game value under the #760 conversion.\n- Leave the original game, parameters, root imports, parent modules, and blueprint unchanged.\n\n### Testing\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/LowDegreeGame.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/LowDegreeGameBridge.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/LowDegreeGameStrategyBridge.lean`\n- `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.LowDegreeGameStrategyBridge`\n- Integrity scan over all three files for `sorry`, `axiom`, forbidden proof-bypass tokens, and stale search/debug commands: empty.\n- `scripts/install_git_hooks.sh --check`; normal pre-commit hooks passed for every milestone.\n- Full `lake build` was not run because the #762 packet explicitly assigns canonical CI and toolchain reconciliation to MAIN.\n\n### Bound strength\n- Exact PMF, predicate, game, projectivity, and strategy-value equalities. No numerical inequality, coefficient loss, degree loss, or exponent loss is introduced.\n\n---\nCloses #762\n",
