+  "body": "### Motivation\n- Issue #763 needs a compact extraction-witness and error vocabulary shared by the qudit and qubit Pauli soundness conclusions.\n- The definitions preserve `thm:pauli` and `cor:pauli-binary` from `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1431-1491`.\n- This PR is stacked on #760 / PR #761 at commit `517b0b605f756c53320b1f5df964cae31885cbdc` and must not merge before that parent passes its normal gates.\n\n### Description\n- Add a 96-line Mathlib-only public module containing the generic finite extraction witness, normalized EPR state, local-isometry tensor action, shuffled ideal state, unsquared state error, and separate Alice/Bob unaveraged squared operator sums.\n- Convert the existing `PauliSoundnessWitness` and `QubitSoundnessWitness` values to the compact witness.\n- Specialize the operator sums to raw `.pauliOutcome` effects and prove exact equalities with `rawPauliOperatorDistanceA/B` and `qubitOperatorDistanceA/B`.\n- Prove exact ideal-state and unsquared state-error equalities, together with exact fixed-basis qudit-to-qubit transport of all three errors.\n\n### Testing\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/Extraction.lean`\n- `lake env lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/ExtractionBridge.lean`\n- `rg -n \"sorry|axiom\" MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/Extraction.lean MIPStarRE/QPBT/Palomar/ExtractionBridge.lean`\n- `scripts/install_git_hooks.sh --check`\n- Pre-commit statement-integrity, proof-evasion, marker, and axiom checks passed for both commits.\n- A full project build was intentionally not run; #763 assigns canonical full CI to MAIN and requests focused Lean/target builds only.\n\n### Statement integrity\n- Paper assumptions: finite local spaces, local isometries, and a unit auxiliary state; no error premise in the witness.\n- Lean assumptions: the same finite-dimensional data, with `Fintype`, `DecidableEq`, and nonempty target-register instances needed to state the concrete vectors and matrices.\n- Paper conclusion vocabulary: one unsquared state norm and two sums over prescribed outcomes of squared operator-action norms.\n- Lean conclusion vocabulary: exactly those three quantities, with qubit sums still indexed by the original field outcomes through the existing fixed basis map.\n- Verdict: exact, with faithful finite-type boundary instances.\n\n### Bound strength\n- `stateError`: stated bound uses the unsquared norm; the definition and bridge give exactly the existing unsquared norm; disposition: sharp.\n- `aliceOperatorError`: stated quantity is the unaveraged sum of squared norms; the bridge gives exactly `rawPauliOperatorDistanceA` or `qubitOperatorDistanceA`; disposition: sharp.\n- `bobOperatorError`: stated quantity is the unaveraged sum of squared norms; the bridge gives exactly `rawPauliOperatorDistanceB` or `qubitOperatorDistanceB`; disposition: sharp.\n- No coefficient, exponent, root, normalization, register-order, or outcome-index loss is introduced.\n\n---\nCloses #763\n",
