 only Mathlib and other\n    34\tgenerated challenge modules. Mirroring the library module partition is\n    35\tnecessary because compiler-generated auxiliary names and instance visibility\n    36\tare module-sensitive.\n    37\t\n    38\t`Solution.lean` imports the four library theorem modules. `comparator.json`\n    39\tnames the four targets and the three permitted axioms. `lakefile.toml` and\n    40\t`lake-manifest.json` pin the exact library revision used to generate the\n    41\tchallenge.\n    42\t\n    43\t## Verification\n    44\t\n    45\tOn Linux with Landlock, Go, a current Rust toolchain, `jq`, and `elan`, run:\n    46\t\n    47\t```sh\n    48\t./verify.sh\n    49\t```\n    50\t\n    51\tThis invokes the unchanged official comparator with real landrun and nanoda.\n    52\tFor diagnostics only, `./verify.sh --fake-landrun` substitutes the comparator's\n    53\tdevelopment sandbox and disables nanoda; that mode is not official acceptance.\n    54\t\n    55\tThe authoritative GitHub workflow checks the Mathlib-only import boundary,\n    56\tthe full revision pin, Lean compilation and kernel replay, then runs the real\n    57\tlandrun/nanoda comparison.\n    58\t\n    59\t## Source Pin\n    60\t\n    61\tThis candidate pins MIPStarRE-A commit\n    62\t`ecb97d1f66eec1e6fad964f144f78b91ce1fab36`, the service-merged PR 671 commit\n    63\ton `main`. The checked-in 31-file challenge is byte-identical to\n    64\t`scripts/comparator/expected/qpbt/` at that source commit.\n    65\t\n    66\t## Regeneration\n    67\t\n    68\tFrom the pinned MIPStarRE-A checkout, run:\n    69\t\n    70\t```sh\n    71\tpython3 scripts/comparator/check_challenge_drift.py \\\n    72\t  --root . --challenge qpbt --update\n    73\t```\n    74\t\n    75\tThen replace this repository's `Challenge.lean` and `Challenge/` with the\n    76\tcontents of `scripts/comparator/expected/qpbt/`, and update the MIPStarRE\n    77\trevision in both Lake files in the same commit.\n--- Challenge.lean\n     1\timport Mathlib\n     2\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.LDT.Basic.ParametersBase\n     3\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries.Polynomials\n     4\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.Coefficients\n     5\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.Subspaces\n     6\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.Quantum.FiniteMatrix.Basic\n     7\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.FieldBasis\n     8\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.Lines\n     9\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.LowDegreeCode\n    10\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.State\n    11\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.Quantum.FiniteMatrix.NormalizedTrace\n    12\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.Pauli\n    13\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.SelfDualBasis\n    14\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.Quantum.Measurement\n    15\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.SelfDualBasisTheorems\n    16\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.LDT.Basic.Distribution\n    17\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Algebra.PauliTheorems\n    18\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.Defs\n    19\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.DistributionAux\n    20\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.CondLinear\n    21\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.Consistency\n    22\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.LowDegreeGame\n    23\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.MagicSquare\n    24\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.TypedCondLinear\n    25\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.PauliBasisTest\n    26\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.SoundnessDefs\n    27\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.StrategyClasses\n    28\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.LowDegreeGameMeasurements\n    29\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Observables.WinImplications.Setup\n    30\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Completeness\n    31\timport Challenge.MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.QubitForm\n    32\t\n    33\t/-!\n    34\t# Challenge: headline theorems of the quantum Pauli basis test\n    35\t\n    36\tSelf-contained comparator challenge for the four registered QPBT headline\n    37\ttheorems: low-degree soundness, completeness of the Pauli basis test, its\n    38\tsoundness theorem, and the qubit-coordinate soundness corollary.\n    39\t\n    40\tThe challenge is **Mathlib-only**: apart from Mathlib it imports nothing but\n    41\tits own modules under `Challenge/`, one for each library module that\n    42\tcontributes to the closure.  Together they re-declare, verbatim and in\n    43\tdependency order, every definition in the transitive closure of the statements\n    44\tof the four theorems; the theorems themselves are stated here with `sorry`.\n    45\tThose modules and their imports mirror the library's own module partition\n    46\tand import graph.  That is not cosmetic: Lean caches a nested proof and\n    47\ta `match` auxiliary *per module*, names it after the first declaration of that\n    48\tmodule that needs it, and lets a declaration see only the instances its\n    49\tmodule's imports bring into scope, while the comparator compares the full\n    50\t`ConstantInfo` of every closure constant, values and proofs included.  A\n    51\tsingle-file challenge therefore cannot reproduce those names whenever the\n    52\tlibrary needs the same fact in two modules; the mirrored partition reproduces\n    53\tthem by construction.\n    54\t\n    55\tThe set of challenge modules is the entire human audit surface: a reader who\n    56\tagrees that they state the intended theorems does not need to read anything\n    57\telse.  The\n    58\t[comparator](https://github.com/leanprover/comparator) tool verifies\n    59\tmechanically that the [MIPStarRE](https://github.com/LionSR/MIPStarRE)\n    60\tlibrary declares statements identical to these and proves the theorems using\n    61\tno axioms beyond `propext`, `Quot.sound`, and `Classical.choice`.\n    62\t\n    63\tEach declaration carries a provenance comment (`-- source: <file>:<lines>`)\n    64\tpointing at its origin in the MIPStarRE library, where docstrings cite the\n    65\tpaper passages being encoded, and each challenge module names the library\n    66\tmodule it mirrors.  These files are generated by\n    67\t`scripts/comparator/` in that repository; see the README alongside this file\n    68\tfor how to run the verification.\n    69\t-/\n    70\t\n    71\topen scoped BigOperators MatrixOrder Matrix ComplexOrder\n    72\t-- Compiler-generated declarations in the closure (no source\n    73\t-- range); they regenerate identically during elaboration:\n    74\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.MsType.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquare.lean)\n    75\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.bind_uniformOnFinset_map._simp_1_3  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistributionAux.lean)\n    76\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.isCompl_registerSubmodule_canonicalComplement._simp_1_4  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n    77\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdType.enumList  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n    78\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.isCompl_registerSubmodule_canonicalComplement._simp_1_6  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n    79\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.isCompl_registerSubmodule_canonicalComplement._simp_1_3  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n    80\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliType.ctorElimType  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n    81\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliAnswer.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n    82\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.prefixRank.eq_1  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n    83\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind.ofNat_ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n    84\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliType.proxyTypeEquiv  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n    85\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdType.ofNat_ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n    86\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.isCompl_registerSubmodule_canonicalComplement._simp_1_5  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n    87\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_self_dual_normal_basis_gal._simp_1_2  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/FieldBasis.lean)\n    88\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.instInhabitedMsType.default  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquare.lean)\n    89\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.trace_group_algebra_pairing._simp_1_2  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/FieldBasis.lean)\n    90\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind.ofNat  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n    91\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.MsAnswer.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquare.lean)\n    92\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.bind_uniformOnFinset_map._simp_1_1  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistributionAux.lean)\n    93\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.normal_basis_trace_dual_apply._simp_1_3  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/FieldBasis.lean)\n    94\t--   MIPStarRE.LDT.Distribution.mk.congr_simp  (from MIPStarRE/LDT/Basic/Distribution.lean)\n    95\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliType.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n    96\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind.enumList  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n    97\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliType.point.inj  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n    98\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.bind_uniformOnFinset_map._simp_1_4  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistributionAux.lean)\n    99\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.Distribution.map_map._simp_1_1  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistributionAux.lean)\n   100\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliAnswer.ctorElimType  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n   101\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.normal_basis_trace_dual_apply._simp_1_2  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/FieldBasis.lean)\n   102\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliType.point.injEq  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/PauliBasisTest.lean)\n   103\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdAnswer.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   104\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind.enumList_nodup  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n   105\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.registerSubmodule_eq_spanSubset._simp_1_2  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n   106\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.instInhabitedLdType.default  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   107\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdType.ofNat  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   108\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdAnswer.ctorElimType  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   109\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.MsType.proxyTypeEquiv  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquare.lean)\n   110\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.registerSubmodule.eq_1  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n   111\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.clDistribution.eq_1  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/CondLinearTheorems.lean)\n   112\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.instInhabitedPauliKind.default  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n   113\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.canonicalComplement.eq_1  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Subspaces.lean)\n   114\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind.enumList_getElem?_ctorIdx_eq  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n   115\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.PauliKind.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Algebra/Pauli.lean)\n   116\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdType.enumList_nodup  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   117\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdType.ctorIdx  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   118\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.bind_uniformOnFinset_map._simp_1_2  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Games/DistributionAux.lean)\n   119\t--   MIPStarRE.QPBT.LdType.enumList_getElem?_ctorIdx_eq  (from MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGame.lean)\n   120\t\n   121\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT\n   122\t\n   123\topen MIPStarRE.LDT MIPStarRE.Quantum\n   124\topen MIPStarRE.LDT.Preliminaries\n   125\t\n   126\t-- source: MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Completeness.lean:263-268\n   127\t--   (MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_spcc_value_one)\n   128\t/-- `lem:pauli-completeness`: every admissible Pauli basis test has a\n   129\tvalue-one SPCC strategy. Blueprint `lem:pauli-completeness`, paper\n   130\t`08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1229-1421`. -/\n   131\ttheorem exists_spcc_value_one (P : AdmissibleParams) :\n   132\t    ∃ S : SymmetricStrategy (pauliBasisTestSymm P),\n   133\t      S.IsSPCC ∧ S.toStrategy.value = 1 := by\n   134\t  sorry\n   135\t\n   136\t-- source: MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGameTheorems.lean:82-108\n   137\t--   (MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_ld_soundness)\n   138\t/-- Quantum soundness of the simultaneous classical low individual degree test.\n   139\tBlueprint `lem:ld-soundness`, paper\n   140\t`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:413-458`. -/\n   141\ttheorem exists_ld_soundness :\n   142\t    ∃ a b : ℝ, 1 ≤ a ∧ 0 < b ∧ b ≤ 1 ∧\n   143\t      ∀ (L : LdParams) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε →\n   144\t        ∀ S : Strategy (ldGame L), S.IsProjective → 1 - ε ≤ S.value →\n   145\t          ∃ GA : PolyMeasTuple L S.ιA, ∃ GB : PolyMeasTuple L S.ιB,\n   146\t            consistencyDefect (uniformDistribution (Fin L.m → ScalarQ L))\n   147\t                (fun u outcome =>\n   148\t                  heteroKron\n   149\t                    (((S.A (ldPointQuestionOf L u)).postprocess\n   150\t                      (ldPointValuesOrZero L)).effect outcome) 1)\n   151\t                (fun u outcome =>\n   152\t                  heteroKron 1\n   153\t                    ((GB.postprocess (evalPolyTupleAt u)).effect outcome))\n   154\t                S.ψ ≤ deltaLd a b ε L.q L.m L.d L.k ∧\n   155\t            consistencyDefect (uniformDistribution (Fin L.m → ScalarQ L))\n   156\t                (fun u outcome =>\n   157\t                  heteroKron\n   158\t                    ((GA.postprocess (evalPolyTupleAt u)).effect outcome) 1)\n   159\t                (fun u outcome =>\n   160\t                  heteroKron 1\n   161\t                    (((S.B (ldPointQuestionOf L u)).postprocess\n   162\t                      (ldPointValuesOrZero L)).effect outcome))\n   163\t                S.ψ ≤ deltaLd a b ε L.q L.m L.d L.k ∧\n   164\t            consistencyDefect (uniformDistribution Unit)\n   165\t                (fun _ g => heteroKron (GA.effect g) 1)\n   166\t                (fun _ g => heteroKron 1 (GB.effect g))\n   167\t                S.ψ ≤ deltaLd a b ε L.q L.m L.d L.k := by\n   168\t  sorry\n   169\t\n   170\t-- source: MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Soundness.lean:40-65  (MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness)\n   171\t/-- `thm:pauli`: every sufficiently successful Pauli basis test strategy admits\n   172\tlocal isometries and an auxiliary unit state for which the state and both\n   173\traw prescribed-answer operator families are close at scale `deltaQld`. The theorem uses the\n   174\tonce-and-for-all self-dual-normal field model selected by `fixedFieldModel` for\n   175\teach admissible size, rather than a freshly quantified field identification.\n   176\tBlueprint\n   177\t`thm:pauli`; paper origin\n   178\t`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1426-1447`.\n   179\t\n   180\tThe paper's asymptotic constants are encoded by the explicit `deltaQld`\n   181\tfunctional; the squared operator distances use the quantitative convention of\n   182\tblueprint `def:povm-distance`.\n   183\t-/\n   184\ttheorem pauli_soundness :\n   185\t    ∃ a b : ℝ, 1 ≤ a ∧ 0 < b ∧ b < 1 ∧\n   186\t      ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ), 0 ≤ ε →\n   187\t        ∀ S : Strategy (pauliBasisTest P), 1 - ε ≤ S.value →\n   188\t          ∃ w : PauliSoundnessWitness P S,\n   189\t            ‖isometryTensor w.φA w.φB S.ψ - idealState P w.aux‖ ≤\n   190\t                deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q ∧\n   191\t            (∀ W : PauliKind,\n   192\t              rawPauliOperatorDistanceA P S w W ≤ deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q) ∧\n   193\t            (∀ W : PauliKind,\n   194\t              rawPauliOperatorDistanceB P S w W ≤ deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q) := by\n   195\t  sorry\n   196\t\n   197\t-- source: MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/QubitForm.lean:411-436  (MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit)\n   198\t/-- `cor:pauli-binary`: soundness of the Pauli basis test in qubit\n   199\tcoordinates. Blueprint `cor:pauli-binary`, paper\n   200\t`08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1450-1491`.\n   201\t\n   202\tThe theorem assumes a nonnegative error parameter, as in the source, and uses\n   203\tonly `P.model` and its stored basis dimension.\n   204\t\n   205\t**Proof dependency:** The coordinate change and all three error identities are\n   206\tproved, and the source theorem `pauli_soundness` is proved as well, so this\n   207\tcorollary is complete: its axiom closure is `propext`, `Classical.choice` and\n   208\t`Quot.sound`. The composition that closed `pauli_soundness` is recorded in\n   209\tissue #614, under the umbrella issue #529. -/\n   210\ttheorem pauli_soundness_qubit :\n   211\t    ∃ a b : ℝ, 1 ≤ a ∧ 0 < b ∧ b < 1 ∧\n   212\t      ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ), 0 ≤ ε →\n   213\t        ∀ S : Strategy (pauliBasisTest P), 1 - ε ≤ S.value →\n   214\t          ∃ w : QubitSoundnessWitness P S,\n   215\t            ‖isometryTensor w.φA w.φB S.ψ - idealQubitState P w.aux‖ ≤\n   216\t                deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q ∧\n   217\t            (∀ W : PauliKind,\n   218\t              qubitOperatorDistanceA P S w W ≤\n   219\t                deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q) ∧\n   220\t            ∀ W : PauliKind,\n   221\t              qubitOperatorDistanceB P S w W ≤\n   222\t                deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q := by\n   223\t  sorry\n   224\t\n   225\tend MIPStarRE.QPBT\n--- Solution.lean\n     1\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Soundness\n     2\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.QubitForm\n     3\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Completeness\n     4\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.LowDegreeGameTheorems\n     5\t\n     6\t/-!\n     7\t# Solution\n     8\t\n     9\tThe MIPStarRE-A library itself proves the four registered QPBT headline\n    10\ttheorems.\n    11\t`Challenge.lean` re-declares the statements' definitional closure verbatim\n    12\tunder the same fully-qualified names, so importing the library is the entire\n    13\tsolution; comparator checks that the two environments declare identical\n    14\tstatements.\n    15\t-/\n--- .github/workflows/comparator.yml\n     1\tname: Comparator verification\n     2\t\n     3\t# Runs the official leanprover/comparator: the MIPStarRE-A library (pinned in\n     4\t# lakefile.toml and lake-manifest.json) proves exactly the statements in\n     5\t# Challenge.lean using only propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice, replayed\n     6\t# through the Lean kernel and the independent nanoda kernel.  The challenge\n     7\t# is Challenge.lean together with the modules under Challenge/.  See the\n     8\t# Validating Proofs chapter of the Lean reference manual for the trust model.\n     9\t#\n    10\t# The systemd-run guard from the comparator README is omitted: it hardens\n    11\t# against landrun escapes by untrusted solutions, and both modules here come\n    12\t# from this trusted checkout.\n    13\t#\n    14\t# This is the authoritative run.  On the development host the sandbox and the\n    15\t# external kernel are unavailable (no Go, no modern Rust), so local runs use\n    16\t# ./verify.sh --fake-landrun and are functional checks only.\n    17\t\n    18\ton:\n    19\t  push:\n    20\t    branches: [main, master, issue-662-closure-20260921-diagnostic]\n    21\t  pull_request:\n    22\t  workflow_dispatch:\n    23\t  schedule:\n    24\t    - cron: '41 5 * * 1'  # weekly: catch upstream tool or cache drift\n    25\t\n    26\tconcurrency:\n    27\t  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n    28\t  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\n    29\t\n    30\tjobs:\n    31\t  comparator:\n    32\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    33\t    timeout-minutes: 360\n    34\t\n    35\t    steps:\n    36\t      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n    37\t\n    38\t      - name: Check the challenge imports only Mathlib and its own modules\n    39\t        run: |\n    40\t          # The challenge is one Mathlib-only module per contributing library\n    41\t          # module (see the README): every module may import Mathlib and other\n    42\t          # Challenge modules, and nothing else -- in particular never the\n    43\t          # library it is meant to be an independent statement of.\n    44\t          files=\"Challenge.lean $(find Challenge -name '*.lean' | sort)\"\n    45\t          bad=$(grep -hE '^import ' $files \\\n    46\t                | grep -vE '^import Mathlib$|^import Challenge(\\.[A-Za-z0-9_.]+)?$' \\\n    47\t                || true)\n    48\t          if [ -n \"$bad\" ]; then\n    49\t            echo \"::error::challenge modules may import only Mathlib and other\"\n    50\t            echo \"::error::challenge modules, found: $bad\"\n    51\t            exit 1\n    52\t          fi\n    53\t          echo \"checked $(printf '%s\\n' $files | wc -l) challenge modules\"\n    54\t\n    55\t      - name: Check the library pin is a full commit hash\n    56\t        run: |\n    57\t          rev=$(grep -E '^rev = ' lakefile.toml | head -1 | sed 's/.*\"\\(.*\\)\"/\\1/')\n    58\t          if ! printf '%s' \"$rev\" | grep -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; then\n    59\t            echo \"::error::lakefile.toml must pin MIPStarRE to a full 40-character commit hash, found: $rev\"\n    60\t            exit 1\n    61\t          fi\n    62\t          man=$(grep -A6 '\"name\": \"MIPStarRE\"' lake-manifest.json | grep '\"rev\"' | head -1 | sed 's/.*\"rev\": \"\\(.*\\)\".*/\\1/')\n    63\t          if [ -n \"$man\" ] && [ \"$man\" != \"$rev\" ]; then\n    64\t            echo \"::error::lakefile.toml pins $rev but lake-manifest.json pins $man\"\n    65\t            exit 1\n    66\t          fi\n    67\t          echo \"library pin: $rev\"\n    68\t\n    69\t      - name: Free disk space before Lean setup\n    70\t        run: |\n    71\t          sudo rm -rf /usr/share/dotnet /usr/local/lib/android /opt/ghc /usr/local/share/boost\n    72\t          if [ -n \"${AGENT_TOOLSDIRECTORY:-}\" ]; then\n    73\t            sudo rm -rf \"$AGENT_TOOLSDIRECTORY\"\n    74\t          fi\n    75\t          df -h\n    76\t\n    77\t      - name: Build Challenge and Solution (with leanchecker re-check)\n    78\t        uses: le