+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show b01bcd297b8063699f0f321e3ef17485f399b0ee:MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/AxiomAudit.lean | nl -ba | sed -n '1,180p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\timport Lean\n     2\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Soundness\n     3\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.QubitForm\n     4\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.QuantitativeSoundness\n     5\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.QuantitativeQubitForm\n     6\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.LowDegreeGameTheorems\n     7\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Completeness\n     8\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Soundness.ProjectiveSetting\n     9\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Soundness.NaimarkAssembly\n    10\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.Soundness.OperatorTransfer\n    11\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Lines\n    12\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Apply\n    13\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.ActualErrorBounds\n    14\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Games.Symmetrization\n    15\t\n    16\t/-!\n    17\t# Axiom audits for the quantum Pauli basis test\n    18\t\n    19\tReviewer-facing, machine-checked evidence that the QPBT headline results rest on\n    20\tnothing beyond Lean's three standard axioms.  Before this module the claim was\n    21\treproducible only by running a throwaway metaprogram outside the repository; a\n    22\treader of the artifact could not re-derive it.\n    23\t\n    24\tEach audit below both **prints** the axiom set of a headline declaration and\n    25\t**fails elaboration** unless that set is exactly\n    26\t\n    27\t`{Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext}`.\n    28\t\n    29\tSo the module is a compile-time regression test, not a report: if a `sorry`\n    30\t(`sorryAx`), a new `axiom` declaration, or any other unexpected dependency ever\n    31\treaches one of these theorems, `lake build MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.AxiomAudit`\n    32\tfails and CI goes red.  The printed lines remain in the build log as the\n    33\tpositive record.\n    34\t\n    35\tThis mirrors `MIPStarRE/LDT/Test/AxiomAudit.lean`, which uses the same\n    36\t`Lean.collectAxioms` mechanism for the classical low-individual-degree track.\n    37\tLike that module, this one is built explicitly as a CI target rather than\n    38\timported from the `MIPStarRE.QPBT` umbrella, so the audits stay out of normal\n    39\tdownstream imports while still acting as regression tests.\n    40\t\n    41\t## What is audited\n    42\t\n    43\tThe declarations are the QPBT headline results, in dependency order from the\n    44\tsoundness statement down to the combining and extraction layers:\n    45\t\n    46\t* `pauli_soundness` — the main theorem (blueprint `thm:pauli`).\n    47\t* `pauli_soundness_qubit` — its qubit form (`cor:pauli-binary`).\n    48\t* `pauli_soundness_explicit_baseline` and\n    49\t  `pauli_soundness_qubit_explicit_baseline` — the Lean-only issue #729\n    50\t  quantitative specializations with fixed current-proof constants.\n    51\t* `pauli_soundness_quantitative` and\n    52\t  `pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative` — the structured degree-four issue #729\n    53\t  bounds, with internally constructed global and extraction witnesses.\n    54\t* `pauli_soundness_quantitative_mixed_components` and its exact qubit form —\n    55\t  the capped squared-state and separate raw-operator component bounds.\n    56\t* `pauli_soundness_quantitative_fractional` and its exact qubit form — the\n    57\t  terminal fractional-dimensional common bound from the native estimates.\n    58\t* `pauli_soundness_quantitative_degree_two` and its exact qubit form — the\n    59\t  sharper degree-two issue #729 bounds, reconstructed on their nonsaturated\n    60\t  branch.\n    61\t* `pauli_soundness_quantitative_canonical` and\n    62\t  `pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative_canonical` — the corresponding canonical\n    63\t  `deltaQld 100` bounds at exponent `1 / 67108864`.\n    64\t* `exists_ld_soundness` — quantum low-degree soundness (`lem:ld-soundness`).\n    65\t* `exists_spcc_value_one` and `honestStrategy_isSPCC` — completeness, which is\n    66\t  what keeps the soundness hypothesis non-vacuous.\n    67\t* `exists_combinedLinesWitness`, `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established`,\n    68\t  `exists_globalPairWitness`, `exists_actual_rounded_global_pair_error_bound`,\n    69\t  and the native quantitative global-pair constructor, fractional comparison,\n    70\t  and legacy comparison — the combining layer.\n    71\t* `exists_projective_setting_isometry_bounds`,\n    72\t  `exists_arbitrary_strategy_isometry_bounds`,\n    73\t  `pauli_soundness_deltaQld_ofExtractionWitness` — the extraction layer.\n    74\t* `exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_approx` — the symmetrization interface.\n    75\t\n    76\t`exists_extendedLinesWitness_established` and\n    77\t`exists_symmetric_projective_strategy_approx` are the two *corrected* forms\n    78\trecorded in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt-gap-register.md`; they are audited here\n    79\tprecisely because they are the statements that were repaired against the source,\n    80\tso a regression in them is the one most likely to go unnoticed.\n    81\t-/\n    82\t\n    83\topen Lean Elab Command\n    84\t\n    85\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.AxiomAudit\n    86\t\n    87\t/-- The axioms Lean's own core development uses, and the only ones a QPBT\n    88\theadline declaration may depend on. -/\n    89\tprivate def standardAxioms : Array Name :=\n    90\t  (#[``propext, ``Classical.choice, ``Quot.sound] : Array Name).qsort Name.lt\n    91\t\n    92\tprivate def resolveDeclIdent (id : TSyntax `ident) : CommandElabM Name := do\n    93\t  liftCoreM <| Lean.Elab.realizeGlobalConstNoOverloadWithInfo id\n    94\t\n    95\tend MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.AxiomAudit\n    96\t\n    97\topen MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.AxiomAudit in\n    98\t/-- Print the axioms of a declaration and fail elaboration unless they are\n    99\texactly `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`.\n   100\t\n   101\tThe failure branch names `sorryAx` explicitly when it is present, because that\n   102\tis the diagnosis a reader wants first: an unexpected `sorryAx` means a proof\n   103\twas left open, while any other extra axiom means a new assumption entered the\n   104\tdevelopment. -/\n   105\telab \"audit_standard_axioms \" id:ident : command => do\n   106\t  let declName ← resolveDeclIdent id\n   107\t  let axioms := (← Lean.collectAxioms declName).qsort Name.lt\n   108\t  logInfo m!\"axioms of '{declName}': {axioms.toList}\"\n   109\t  unless axioms == standardAxioms do\n   110\t    if axioms.contains ``sorryAx then\n   111\t      throwError\n   112\t        m!\"'{declName}' depends on `sorryAx`: a proof it relies on is still \" ++\n   113\t          m!\"open.  Axioms: {axioms.toList}\"\n   114\t    else\n   115\t      throwError\n   116\t        m!\"'{declName}' depends on axioms {axioms.toList}, expected exactly \" ++\n   117\t          m!\"{standardAxioms.toList}\"\n   118\t\n   119\t/-! ### Main theorem and its qubit form -/\n   120\t\n   121\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness\n   122\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit\n   123\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_explicit_baseline\n   124\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_explicit_baseline\n   125\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative\n   126\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_canonical\n   127\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative\n   128\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative_canonical\n   129\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_mixed_components\n   130\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative_mixed_components\n   131\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_fractional\n   132\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative_fractional\n   133\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_degree_two\n   134\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_qubit_quantitative_degree_two\n   135\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_power_eq_gain_mul_baseline\n   136\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_envelope_pos\n   137\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.sqrt_quantitative_extraction_scale_le\n   138\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.sqrt_quantitative_extraction_scale_le_degree_two\n   139\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.quantitative_ratio_le_degree_two_base\n   140\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.quantitative_error_le_degree_two_base\n   141\taudit_standard_axioms\n   142\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.quantitative_ratio_lt_four_billionth_of_degree_two_raw_lt_four\n   143\taudit_standard_axioms\n   144\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.sqrt_quantitative_extraction_scale_lt_four_thousandths\n   145\taudit_standard_axioms\n   146\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.quantitative_extraction_scale_lt_one_of_degree_two_raw_lt_four\n   147\taudit_standard_axioms\n   148\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.quantitative_state_component_lt_degree_two_raw_error\n   149\taudit_standard_axioms\n   150\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.quantitative_operator_component_lt_degree_two_raw_error\n   151\taudit_standard_axioms\n   152\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_degree_two_error_le_quantitative_error\n   153\taudit_standard_axioms\n   154\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_fractional_error_le_degree_two\n   155\taudit_standard_axioms\n   156\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_degree_two_error_lt_quantitative_error_iff\n   157\taudit_standard_axioms\n   158\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_degree_two_error_le_deltaQld\n   159\taudit_standard_axioms MIPStarRE.QPBT.deltaQld_quantitative_lt_explicit_baseline\n   160\taudit_standard_axioms\n   161\t  MIPStarRE.QPBT.pauli_soundness_quantitative_error_lt_explicit_baseline_clip