+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show 32d9e248b4086b6e2f829d68b2effc9ce7b47be5:formalization.yaml | nl -ba | sed -n '1,220p'; git show 32d9e248b4086b6e2f829d68b2effc9ce7b47be5:.github/workflows/comparator.yml | nl -ba | sed -n '1,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\tversion: \"v0.4\"\n     2\t\n     3\tproject:\n     4\t  name: \"Quantum Pauli basis test\"\n     5\t  description: >-\n     6\t    A Lean 4 formalization of the quantum Pauli basis test from MIP*=RE. The\n     7\t    registered results give a value-one symmetric projective consistent\n     8\t    commuting strategy, quantum soundness of the simultaneous low-degree\n     9\t    test, soundness of the Pauli basis test up to local isometries with the\n    10\t    explicit deltaQld error, and the corresponding qubit-coordinate form.\n    11\t  authors:\n    12\t    - \"Ruixuan Deng\"\n    13\t  responsible_maintainers:\n    14\t    - \"Ruixuan Deng\"\n    15\t  license: \"Apache-2.0\"\n    16\t\n    17\trepository:\n    18\t  role: \"thin-wrapper\"\n    19\t  substantive_formalization:\n    20\t    id: \"Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-QPBT\"\n    21\t    revision: \"ecb97d1f66eec1e6fad964f144f78b91ce1fab36\"\n    22\t\n    23\tclassification:\n    24\t  arxiv:\n    25\t    - \"quant-ph\"\n    26\t  msc2020: []\n    27\t\n    28\tsources:\n    29\t  - type: \"article\"\n    30\t    title: \"MIP*=RE\"\n    31\t    authors:\n    32\t      - \"Zhengfeng Ji\"\n    33\t      - \"Anand Natarajan\"\n    34\t      - \"Thomas Vidick\"\n    35\t      - \"John Wright\"\n    36\t      - \"Henry Yuen\"\n    37\t    id: \"arXiv:2001.04383\"\n    38\t    relationship: \"formalizes\"\n    39\t    location: >-\n    40\t      Section 4.7, including lem:ld-soundness, lem:pauli-completeness,\n    41\t      thm:pauli, and cor:pauli-binary; the analysis continues in Section 8.\n    42\t    author_endorsement: \"not-contacted\"\n    43\t\n    44\tstatus:\n    45\t  scope: >-\n    46\t    The comparator registers four headline declarations: completeness of the\n    47\t    Pauli basis test, soundness of the simultaneous low-degree test, Pauli\n    48\t    basis test soundness, and its qubit form.\n    49\t  main_results:\n    50\t    - name: \"Pauli basis test completeness\"\n    51\t      declaration: \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_spcc_value_one\"\n    52\t      file: \"MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Completeness.lean\"\n    53\t      comparator_config: \"comparator.json\"\n    54\t    - name: \"Simultaneous low-degree test soundness\"\n    55\t      declaration: \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_ld_soundness\"\n    56\t      file: \"MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/LowDegreeGameTheorems.lean\"\n    57\t      comparator_config: \"comparator.json\"\n    58\t    - name: \"Pauli basis test soundness\"\n    59\t      declaration: \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.pauli_soundness\"\n    60\t      file: \"MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/Soundness.lean\"\n    61\t      comparator_config: \"comparator.json\"\n    62\t    - name: \"Qubit-coordinate Pauli soundness\"\n    63\t      declaration: \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.pauli_soundness_qubit\"\n    64\t      file: \"MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/QubitForm.lean\"\n    65\t      comparator_config: \"comparator.json\"\n    66\t  declarations:\n    67\t    - \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_spcc_value_one\"\n    68\t    - \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.exists_ld_soundness\"\n    69\t    - \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.pauli_soundness\"\n    70\t    - \"MIPStarRE.QPBT.Palomar.pauli_soundness_qubit\"\n    71\t\n    72\talignment:\n    73\t  source_statement: \"other\"\n    74\t  translation_notes: >-\n    75\t    The four registered declarations retain the current comparator candidate's\n    76\t    parameter order, quantifier order, witnesses, and explicit deltaLd or\n    77\t    deltaQld error forms. The substantive repository documents proof-route and\n    78\t    printed-source corrections separately. This draft makes no independent\n    79\t    equivalence or faithfulness claim; comparator equality alone would not\n    80\t    establish one.\n    81\t\n    82\tautomation:\n    83\t  methods:\n    84\t    - method: \"agent\"\n    85\t      framework: \"MIPStarRE-dev local coding-agent workflow\"\n    86\t      tool_setup: >-\n    87\t        AI coding agents edited Lean, documentation, and repository tooling;\n    88\t        deterministic local scripts, Lean, and the official comparator were\n    89\t        used for mechanical checks at recorded snapshots.\n    90\t  notes: >-\n    91\t    This work is AI-generated. Ruixuan Deng is the responsible owner and made\n    92\t    the recorded project decisions. No human review beyond those owner\n    93\t    decisions is claimed by this metadata draft.\n    94\t\n    95\treview:\n    96\t  status: \"unchecked\"\n    97\t  reviewers: []\n    98\t  notes: >-\n    99\t    No human mathematical or code review is claimed. Automated agent reviews\n   100\t    and historical comparator runs are not represented as human approval.\n     1\tname: Comparator verification\n     2\t\n     3\t# Runs the official leanprover/comparator: the MIPStarRE-A library (pinned in\n     4\t# lakefile.toml and lake-manifest.json) proves exactly the statements in\n     5\t# Challenge.lean using only propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice, replayed\n     6\t# through the Lean kernel and the independent nanoda kernel.  The challenge\n     7\t# is Challenge.lean together with the modules under Challenge/.  See the\n     8\t# Validating Proofs chapter of the Lean reference manual for the trust model.\n     9\t#\n    10\t# The systemd-run guard from the comparator README is omitted: it hardens\n    11\t# against landrun escapes by untrusted solutions, and both modules here come\n    12\t# from this trusted checkout.\n    13\t#\n    14\t# This is the authoritative run.  On the development host the sandbox and the\n    15\t# external kernel are unavailable (no Go, no modern Rust), so local runs use\n    16\t# ./verify.sh --fake-landrun and are functional checks only.\n    17\t\n    18\ton:\n    19\t  push:\n    20\t    branches: [main, master, issue-662-closure-20260921-diagnostic]\n    21\t  pull_request:\n    22\t  workflow_dispatch:\n    23\t  schedule:\n    24\t    - cron: '41 5 * * 1'  # weekly: catch upstream tool or cache drift\n    25\t\n    26\tconcurrency:\n    27\t  group: ${{ github.workflow }}-${{ github.ref }}\n    28\t  cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\n    29\t\n    30\tjobs:\n    31\t  comparator:\n    32\t    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    33\t    timeout-minutes: 360\n    34\t\n    35\t    steps:\n    36\t      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n    37\t\n    38\t      - name: Check the challenge imports only Mathlib and its own modules\n    39\t        run: |\n    40\t          # The challenge is one Mathlib-only module per contributing library\n    41\t          # module (see the README): every module may import Mathlib and other\n    42\t          # Challenge modules, and nothing else -- in particular never the\n    43\t          # library it is meant to be an independent statement of.\n    44\t          files=\"Challenge.lean $(find Challenge -name '*.lean' | sort)\"\n    45\t          bad=$(grep -hE '^import ' $files \\\n    46\t                | grep -vE '^import Mathlib$|^import Challenge(\\.[A-Za-z0-9_.]+)?$' \\\n    47\t                || true)\n    48\t          if [ -n \"$bad\" ]; then\n    49\t            echo \"::error::challenge modules may import only Mathlib and other\"\n    50\t            echo \"::error::challenge modules, found: $bad\"\n    51\t            exit 1\n    52\t          fi\n    53\t          echo \"checked $(printf '%s\\n' $files | wc -l) challenge modules\"\n    54\t\n    55\t      - name: Check the library pin is a full commit hash\n    56\t        run: |\n    57\t          rev=$(grep -E '^rev = ' lakefile.toml | head -1 | sed 's/.*\"\\(.*\\)\"/\\1/')\n    58\t          if ! printf '%s' \"$rev\" | grep -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; then\n    59\t            echo \"::error::lakefile.toml must pin MIPStarRE to a full 40-character commit hash, found: $rev\"\n    60\t            exit 1\n    61\t          fi\n    62\t          man=$(grep -A6 '\"name\": \"MIPStarRE\"' lake-manifest.json | grep '\"rev\"' | head -1 | sed 's/.*\"rev\": \"\\(.*\\)\".*/\\1/')\n    63\t          if [ -n \"$man\" ] && [ \"$man\" != \"$rev\" ]; then\n    64\t            echo \"::error::lakefile.toml pins $rev but lake-manifest.json pins $man\"\n    65\t            exit 1\n    66\t          fi\n    67\t          echo \"library pin: $rev\"\n    68\t\n    69\t      - name: Free disk space before Lean setup\n    70\t        run: |\n    71\t          sudo rm -rf /usr/share/dotnet /usr/local/lib/android /opt/ghc /usr/local/share/boost\n    72\t          if [ -n \"${AGENT_TOOLSDIRECTORY:-}\" ]; then\n    73\t            sudo rm -rf \"$AGENT_TOOLSDIRECTORY\"\n    74\t          fi\n    75\t          df -h\n    76\t\n    77\t      - name: Build Challenge and Solution (with leanchecker re-check)\n    78\t        uses: leanprover/lean-action@v1\n    79\t        with:\n    80\t          leanchecker: true\n    81\t\n    82\t      - name: Set up Go for landrun\n    83\t        uses: actions/setup-go@v6\n    84\t        with:\n    85\t          go-version: stable\n    86\t          cache: false\n    87\t\n    88\t      - name: Cache verification tools\n    89\t        uses: actions/cache@v4\n    90\t        with:\n    91\t          path: |\n    92\t            landrun/landrun\n    93\t            comparator/.lake\n    94\t            nanoda_lib/target/release/nanoda_bin\n    95\t          key: comparator-tools-${{ hashFiles('lean-toolchain', 'verify.sh') }}\n    96\t\n    97\t      - name: Run comparator\n    98\t        run: ./verify.sh\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
