12:   112\tsubject to the Solution axiom audit.\n113-   113\t\n114-   114\tThis old four-statement tree still exceeds Palomar's 1,000-line and 100-KiB hard\n115-   115\tlimits.  It is evidence for the definition frontier, not the final single-file\n116-   116\tChallenge or a readiness claim; the compact statement/bridge work remains\n117-   117\tseparate.\n--\n137-   137\t\n138-   138\tRun the deterministic guard from the repository root (requires a built\n139-   139\tlibrary).  With no `--challenge` every configured challenge is checked:\n140-   140\t\n141-   141\t```sh\n142:   142\tpython3 scripts/comparator/check_challenge_drift.py --root .\n143:   143\tpython3 scripts/comparator/check_challenge_drift.py --root . --challenge qpbt\n144:   144\tpython3 scripts/comparator/check_challenge_drift.py --root . --challenge palomar\n145-   145\t```\n146-   146\t\n147-   147\tAdd `--challenge <name>` (repeatable) to restrict the run to one challenge.\n148-   148\t\n149-   149\tTo update a checked-in expected copy after an intentional statement or\n150-   150\tdependency change, run the exact maintenance command:\n151-   151\t\n152-   152\t```sh\n153:   153\tpython3 scripts/comparator/check_challenge_drift.py --root . --update\n154-   154\t```\n155-   155\t\n156-   156\tThat command refuses a challenge whose configured header or footer file is not\n157-   157\tin the tree, and reports it as an error while still updating the others: the\n158-   158\tcopy it would write omits those statements, and once such a copy exists the\n159:   159\t`require_expected: false` skip no longer applies, so every later drift run\n160-   160\twould report a challenge that states nothing as current.\n161-   161\t\n162-   162\tThe regeneration guard and the LDT preservation regression answer different\n163-   163\tquestions.  Regeneration checks that the fixture agrees with the current\n164-   164\tlibrary.  `ComparatorChallengeDriftTests.test_ldt_expected_matches_baseline`\n--\n174-   174\tunchan